1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,098
It's 13 to 19, a six-point difference.

2
00:00:02,121 --> 00:00:03,131
We're in the lead,

3
00:00:03,448 --> 00:00:04,692
but we can't let our guard down.

4
00:00:04,783 --> 00:00:07,747
(Wonder Dogs need to dominate early.)

5
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:10,245
Song Hee, aim for the gap.

6
00:00:10,269 --> 00:00:11,980
And where do you hit high sets?

7
00:00:12,004 --> 00:00:14,115
I told you. Hit it deep.

8
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:15,551
It's okay. Go for it.

9
00:00:16,175 --> 00:00:17,252
(Nodding)

10
00:00:17,543 --> 00:00:19,755
(Hyeon Ju's serve)

11
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:22,958
- My ball!
- Hye In received well.

12
00:00:23,082 --> 00:00:23,792
Hit it!

13
00:00:24,183 --> 00:00:25,093
They hit it!

14
00:00:25,851 --> 00:00:27,020
They saved it.

15
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:29,255
- Enkhsoyol!
- Enkhsoyol's on it!

16
00:00:29,461 --> 00:00:30,338
Hit it!

17
00:00:30,923 --> 00:00:32,934
(A gap is spotted.)

18
00:00:33,292 --> 00:00:35,036
(Aiming for the gap)

19
00:00:35,328 --> 00:00:37,206
Song Hee scores with a spike!

20
00:00:38,164 --> 00:00:40,242
- Nice job, Song Hee.
- Nice one.

21
00:00:41,701 --> 00:00:43,779
(Just as the opposing middle blocker
hesitated,)

22
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:45,814
(she hit the ball in between.)

23
00:00:45,838 --> 00:00:46,581
Okay!

24
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,850
(A tactic against Suwon Special City)

25
00:00:48,874 --> 00:00:51,152
(Aiming for the gap
between the blockers...)

26
00:00:51,344 --> 00:00:53,656
(and spiking right through the gap)

27
00:00:54,647 --> 00:00:57,759
(The tactic has worked all game long.)

28
00:00:59,685 --> 00:01:02,364
The Wonder Dogs are executing
their coach's strategy perfectly.

29
00:01:03,356 --> 00:01:05,601
The Wonder Dogs are leading
by seven points.

30
00:01:08,343 --> 00:01:10,922
(Seung Ju gets ready to serve)

31
00:01:11,263 --> 00:01:12,106
(Whistle blows)

32
00:01:13,966 --> 00:01:15,644
- Serve.
- Isn't it Song Hee's serve?

33
00:01:16,736 --> 00:01:18,981
Isn't it Song Hee's serve?

34
00:01:19,004 --> 00:01:19,848
What?

35
00:01:21,907 --> 00:01:23,551
Isn't it Song Hee's serve?

36
00:01:24,076 --> 00:01:25,520
It's Song Hee's turn.

37
00:01:26,946 --> 00:01:27,723
It's Song Hee's serve.

38
00:01:27,724 --> 00:01:28,968
(Everyone got mixed up on the rotation.)

39
00:01:29,515 --> 00:01:30,617
(The referee blew the whistle.)

40
00:01:30,618 --> 00:01:33,061
The referee already gave the signal.

41
00:01:35,421 --> 00:01:36,331
It's Song Hee's turn!

42
00:01:36,522 --> 00:01:39,201
- Hit it right away!
- Hit it!

43
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:42,871
(Timeout)

44
00:01:42,895 --> 00:01:44,773
- Oh, no.
- Time's up for them.

45
00:01:44,797 --> 00:01:48,043
They lost track of who's serving next.

46
00:01:48,534 --> 00:01:50,645
Darn it!

47
00:01:50,836 --> 00:01:53,281
(A careless point conceded)

48
00:01:53,305 --> 00:01:55,183
The players mixed up their rotation...

49
00:01:55,207 --> 00:01:57,719
- and lost their eight seconds to serve.
- Sorry.

50
00:01:59,812 --> 00:02:01,723
(Second set, Suwon Special City 14
: Wonder Dogs 20)

51
00:02:03,249 --> 00:02:04,526
(The game continues.)

52
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:05,560
Right-side attack!

53
00:02:06,252 --> 00:02:07,362
The ball is set high.

54
00:02:08,487 --> 00:02:09,197
Net touch!

55
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,435
- Oh, no, Sol.
- Sol touched the antenna.

56
00:02:13,459 --> 00:02:14,503
Sorry. My bad.

57
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:18,907
This is bad.

58
00:02:18,931 --> 00:02:20,776
(Tension rising as errors pile up)

59
00:02:23,102 --> 00:02:25,547
(Captain Pyo tries to regain momentum,)

60
00:02:26,172 --> 00:02:28,050
(but makes a service error.)

61
00:02:29,975 --> 00:02:31,653
(Glancing)

62
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:33,688
(Looking away)

63
00:02:34,547 --> 00:02:36,358
(This isn't good.)

64
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,059
(In the previous games...)

65
00:02:38,384 --> 00:02:39,861
What's going on with you guys?

66
00:02:41,954 --> 00:02:44,232
(Coach Yeon Koung never tolerated
errors or mistakes.)

67
00:02:44,256 --> 00:02:45,567
I just had a talk with the producer.

68
00:02:46,058 --> 00:02:51,606
(The rookie coach even suggested
a release system.)

69
00:02:52,164 --> 00:02:54,776
The players need
to regain their composure.

70
00:02:55,768 --> 00:02:57,145
It's raining service errors.

71
00:02:57,169 --> 00:02:59,781
(The rookie coach is about to lose it.)

72
00:03:00,673 --> 00:03:02,384
We're still winning,
so I can keep my smile.

73
00:03:02,675 --> 00:03:04,019
(Laughing)

74
00:03:04,243 --> 00:03:07,622
(What a relief.)

75
00:03:08,314 --> 00:03:10,626
Captain Pyo is trying to read
the coach's face.

76
00:03:10,783 --> 00:03:12,094
It's okay. Don't worry.

77
00:03:12,318 --> 00:03:13,962
(Second set, Suwon Special City 16
: Wonder Dogs 21)

78
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,031
Let's go, Wonder Dogs!

79
00:03:16,055 --> 00:03:18,367
- To the left, girls.
- Okay.

80
00:03:18,791 --> 00:03:20,602
(Bo Been's serve)

81
00:03:22,027 --> 00:03:23,404
My ball!

82
00:03:24,196 --> 00:03:25,106
Sol.

83
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:28,043
(Finds a gap...)

84
00:03:28,067 --> 00:03:29,311
(and spikes it!)

85
00:03:29,335 --> 00:03:30,245
Nice!

86
00:03:30,903 --> 00:03:31,713
Spike!

87
00:03:31,737 --> 00:03:33,404
(Enkhsoyol breaking the chain of errors)

88
00:03:33,405 --> 00:03:35,149
They can win back points right away.

89
00:03:35,441 --> 00:03:37,319
(Second set, Suwon Special City 16
: Wonder Dogs 22)

90
00:03:37,343 --> 00:03:38,287
Can you set a bit higher?

91
00:03:39,211 --> 00:03:40,355
- Nice job.
- Okay.

92
00:03:40,379 --> 00:03:41,690
Let's go! One more!

93
00:03:42,348 --> 00:03:43,792
(The game continues.)

94
00:03:43,816 --> 00:03:44,693
A standing spike!

95
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:45,693
Block it!

96
00:03:45,718 --> 00:03:47,596
(Successfully blocks the ball)

97
00:03:48,487 --> 00:03:49,431
Hyeon Ju sets it.

98
00:03:49,922 --> 00:03:51,233
(Where is the ball headed now?)

99
00:03:51,423 --> 00:03:52,834
(Toward Hyeon Ju)

100
00:03:52,892 --> 00:03:53,835
Watch the middle.

101
00:03:54,193 --> 00:03:54,970
Cross!

102
00:03:58,564 --> 00:04:00,742
Spikes, and it's blocked!

103
00:04:00,766 --> 00:04:03,578
Enkhsoyol's perfect block!

104
00:04:03,602 --> 00:04:04,979
A solo block!

105
00:04:05,271 --> 00:04:06,714
Enkhsoyol did it!

106
00:04:06,739 --> 00:04:09,217
Enkhsoyol just made a perfect block.

107
00:04:09,926 --> 00:04:11,570
(Feeling proud)

108
00:04:13,637 --> 00:04:15,649
(Perfectly blocked it
in between her hands)

109
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:18,451
Enkhsoyol and Seung Ju have been...

110
00:04:18,475 --> 00:04:20,620
blocking Hyeon Ju's spikes,

111
00:04:20,644 --> 00:04:23,556
which means Suwon Special City has
no right-side attack right now.

112
00:04:23,581 --> 00:04:24,358
That's right.

113
00:04:24,982 --> 00:04:26,828
When I land one good hit,

114
00:04:26,852 --> 00:04:29,430
my body warms up and I get in the zone.

115
00:04:29,587 --> 00:04:31,098
If I can keep this up,

116
00:04:31,422 --> 00:04:32,332
I'll play well the whole game.

117
00:04:32,823 --> 00:04:34,170
I'll do well.

118
00:04:34,959 --> 00:04:36,136
Go, Song Hee.

119
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,505
Song Hee's receive is on point,
and a back toss.

120
00:04:38,829 --> 00:04:40,240
Enkhsoyol!

121
00:04:40,564 --> 00:04:42,108
(Scoring back-to-back)

122
00:04:42,132 --> 00:04:44,844
Enkhsoyol's been playing really well,

123
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:46,212
including defense.

124
00:04:46,637 --> 00:04:48,615
Since Wonder Dogs was founded,

125
00:04:48,639 --> 00:04:50,150
who's gotten scolded the most so far?

126
00:04:50,174 --> 00:04:51,018
Enkhsoyol.

127
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:52,852
Who was always so down?

128
00:04:52,876 --> 00:04:54,721
- Enkhsoyol.
- Yes, that's right.

129
00:04:54,745 --> 00:04:57,557
And look at her now.
She's Coach Yeon Koung's new ace.

130
00:04:57,575 --> 00:04:58,385
Absolutely.
(The new ace of Wonder Dogs)

131
00:05:00,674 --> 00:05:02,719
It's the set point for Wonder Dogs.

132
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,664
(Set point for the second set)

133
00:05:04,722 --> 00:05:06,600
- Just one more point, please.
- Yes.

134
00:05:06,624 --> 00:05:07,935
(Only one more point to take the set)

135
00:05:08,025 --> 00:05:09,235
Let's finish this set strong.

136
00:05:10,327 --> 00:05:12,805
(Enkhsoyol's serve)

137
00:05:12,963 --> 00:05:14,274
One, two, three.

138
00:05:14,275 --> 00:05:15,953
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

139
00:05:17,434 --> 00:05:18,411
One, two!

140
00:05:18,836 --> 00:05:20,180
- Go!
- I'm coming!

141
00:05:20,237 --> 00:05:21,080
It's set.

142
00:05:21,105 --> 00:05:22,482
(Hyo Rim's hand...)

143
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:24,685
(has crossed
into Wonder Dogs' side of the net.)

144
00:05:25,042 --> 00:05:26,086
It's an over-net!

145
00:05:27,311 --> 00:05:29,757
(She committed an over-net.)

146
00:05:29,781 --> 00:05:30,791
An over-net!

147
00:05:31,415 --> 00:05:34,294
(Enkhsoyol's powerful serve)

148
00:05:34,552 --> 00:05:37,831
Enkhsoyol's powerful serve
made the opponents lose their focus.

149
00:05:39,723 --> 00:05:42,335
(The second set ended
with Wonder Dogs' win.)

150
00:05:43,327 --> 00:05:45,772
The second set is now over, 25 to 18.

151
00:05:45,963 --> 00:05:48,475
Wonder Dogs take the second set as well!

152
00:05:48,487 --> 00:05:50,532
(Second set, Suwon Special City 18
: Wonder Dogs 25)

153
00:05:50,533 --> 00:05:54,313
(Tactical timeout before the third set)

154
00:05:54,705 --> 00:05:58,788
- Hyeon Ju, your success rate is zero.
- Yes, coach.

155
00:05:59,210 --> 00:06:00,254
- Are you aware?
- Yes, coach.

156
00:06:01,612 --> 00:06:05,559
You've got to find your hitting point,
maybe off their hands,

157
00:06:05,783 --> 00:06:08,028
to raise your success rate.

158
00:06:08,029 --> 00:06:08,873
Yes, coach.

159
00:06:08,874 --> 00:06:09,951
(Aiming for the blockers' hands)

160
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:12,065
Both the first and second sets were...

161
00:06:12,590 --> 00:06:14,034
won by Wonder Dogs.

162
00:06:14,035 --> 00:06:15,613
The set score is now two to zero.

163
00:06:15,926 --> 00:06:18,471
I hope they can keep the momentum
from the last game...

164
00:06:18,472 --> 00:06:20,784
and win in straight sets again.

165
00:06:20,785 --> 00:06:21,662
Absolutely.

166
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:23,376
Serve.

167
00:06:23,534 --> 00:06:24,478
Third set beginning.

168
00:06:25,369 --> 00:06:26,413
One, two!

169
00:06:26,437 --> 00:06:27,281
My ball!

170
00:06:27,705 --> 00:06:29,216
(A shaky receive)

171
00:06:29,217 --> 00:06:30,394
That was a shaky receive.

172
00:06:30,808 --> 00:06:32,719
Hit it! Spike!

173
00:06:32,967 --> 00:06:33,710
(She didn't spike it.)

174
00:06:33,711 --> 00:06:35,088
(She played a soft tip.)

175
00:06:35,713 --> 00:06:37,190
A soft tip!

176
00:06:37,191 --> 00:06:38,324
(And she scores.)

177
00:06:38,616 --> 00:06:40,394
- Are you kidding me?
- Sorry.

178
00:06:40,395 --> 00:06:41,639
Come on.

179
00:06:42,019 --> 00:06:43,730
I'd love to ask her...

180
00:06:43,731 --> 00:06:45,842
if she actually saw the defense shift.

181
00:06:45,990 --> 00:06:48,001
If she played that tip
because she saw the gap.

182
00:06:48,326 --> 00:06:50,570
She's been showing
a lot of similar plays today.

183
00:06:50,571 --> 00:06:53,884
If all of those were intentional,
it means Enkhsoyol has definitely evolved.

184
00:06:53,931 --> 00:06:54,941
That's right.

185
00:06:54,942 --> 00:06:57,076
(Tip Enkhsoyol is still evolving.)

186
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:57,910
Seung Ju!

187
00:06:58,802 --> 00:07:01,204
How soft should the serve be for you?

188
00:07:01,205 --> 00:07:03,250
- Okay, coach.
- They hit them like this!

189
00:07:03,408 --> 00:07:05,385
- Okay, coach.
- Just hit it hard.

190
00:07:05,825 --> 00:07:06,634
Serve.

191
00:07:06,635 --> 00:07:08,346
(Next up to serve is Tip Enkhsoyol)

192
00:07:09,813 --> 00:07:10,777
A fast serve.

193
00:07:10,778 --> 00:07:12,175
(Where's the ball set?)

194
00:07:12,383 --> 00:07:13,093
Go!

195
00:07:13,094 --> 00:07:15,039
(Attackers from both sides rushing in)

196
00:07:15,519 --> 00:07:17,897
(Hesitating which way to go)

197
00:07:19,023 --> 00:07:21,935
(The answer was the left side.)

198
00:07:22,459 --> 00:07:23,236
Spike!

199
00:07:23,237 --> 00:07:25,762
(Scores using a play
to confuse the defense)

200
00:07:25,763 --> 00:07:28,175
Yeon Jae has been a strong presence,

201
00:07:28,176 --> 00:07:30,233
scoring five points each
in the first and second sets.

202
00:07:30,234 --> 00:07:33,380
She scored 10 points in the previous sets,
and now she's at 11.

203
00:07:33,637 --> 00:07:35,515
What do you do when Myeong Hwa
and Seung Ju are there?

204
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,819
Hyeon Ju's run-up will be a fake.

205
00:07:38,819 --> 00:07:42,170
If Hyeon Ju sprints,
Myeong Hwa will stay put.

206
00:07:42,171 --> 00:07:43,203
(In the previous tactical timeout)

207
00:07:43,514 --> 00:07:45,525
(They all thought Hyeon Ju was running up
to hit the ball.)

208
00:07:45,549 --> 00:07:49,162
Myeong Hwa had been watching
for the sets going to Hyeon Ju...

209
00:07:49,163 --> 00:07:50,497
- and moved to defend.
- Right.

210
00:07:50,498 --> 00:07:51,498
(Spiked into the open spot)

211
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:54,201
(A tight battle of wits)

212
00:07:54,591 --> 00:07:56,803
(Come on, Myeong Hwa!)

213
00:07:57,161 --> 00:07:58,872
- They moved early.
- Got it.

214
00:07:58,896 --> 00:08:00,440
Stay patient.
They're attacking from both sides.

215
00:08:00,464 --> 00:08:01,408
Okay. Got it.

216
00:08:01,865 --> 00:08:03,242
- Serve.
- It's now 1 to 1.

217
00:08:03,267 --> 00:08:04,978
(Ace Yeon Jae's serve)

218
00:08:05,035 --> 00:08:05,945
One, two!

219
00:08:07,004 --> 00:08:07,948
My ball!

220
00:08:09,473 --> 00:08:10,784
My ball!

221
00:08:11,342 --> 00:08:12,252
One, two!

222
00:08:13,377 --> 00:08:15,522
It drops inside the line!

223
00:08:15,713 --> 00:08:17,724
- Don't dodge. Never dodge.
- Okay.

224
00:08:18,948 --> 00:08:20,450
Service ace by Yeon Jae!

225
00:08:20,451 --> 00:08:23,915
That's right. Suwon Special City has
nothing to lose now,

226
00:08:23,915 --> 00:08:27,233
so they'll probably bring out faster,
stronger serves now.

227
00:08:27,458 --> 00:08:29,102
It's now tied at two-all.

228
00:08:29,828 --> 00:08:30,694
(Time to push ahead now)

229
00:08:30,694 --> 00:08:31,804
Ball, please.

230
00:08:34,398 --> 00:08:36,243
(Yeon Koung gives the service queen
her target.)

231
00:08:36,266 --> 00:08:37,043
Myeong Hwa!

232
00:08:38,235 --> 00:08:40,747
(The target zone for the serve)

233
00:08:40,904 --> 00:08:43,106
I hope she shows them
what an ace serve really is.

234
00:08:43,106 --> 00:08:44,016
(Service queen serves)

235
00:08:45,809 --> 00:08:47,120
A shaky receive.

236
00:08:48,779 --> 00:08:50,757
Spike! And Myeong Hwa digs it!

237
00:08:51,215 --> 00:08:51,992
(Now to Seung Ju)

238
00:08:52,583 --> 00:08:53,784
A soft tip!

239
00:08:53,784 --> 00:08:54,861
(Playing soft tip)

240
00:08:55,619 --> 00:08:56,529
They set it up.

241
00:08:57,388 --> 00:08:58,465
Hyeon Ju's running up again.

242
00:08:58,465 --> 00:09:00,133
(Hyeon Ju running to attack)

243
00:09:00,557 --> 00:09:04,270
We'll block Hyeon Ju's attacks
between your hands.

244
00:09:04,795 --> 00:09:06,773
(Are you ready, Suwon?)

245
00:09:07,064 --> 00:09:11,663
(A new tactic: Aiming for an out,
off the blockers' hands)

246
00:09:12,069 --> 00:09:13,179
Go!

247
00:09:14,638 --> 00:09:15,515
Spike!

248
00:09:17,107 --> 00:09:19,185
(Out of bounds)

249
00:09:19,543 --> 00:09:20,310
(Oh, gosh.)

250
00:09:21,426 --> 00:09:22,550
(Coach Kang's strategy worked.)

251
00:09:22,550 --> 00:09:23,951
- Great.
- Let's go!

252
00:09:23,951 --> 00:09:26,196
Hyeon Ju is indeed the ace player
of Suwon Special City.

253
00:09:26,654 --> 00:09:29,190
Their attacks kept getting caught
by the defense...

254
00:09:29,190 --> 00:09:30,834
and blocks,

255
00:09:31,192 --> 00:09:33,461
but this time,
she aimed long and hit through.

256
00:09:33,461 --> 00:09:37,274
(She varied the attack
with a controlled hit this time.)

257
00:09:37,665 --> 00:09:39,567
(The game continues.)

258
00:09:39,567 --> 00:09:40,210
Tipping.

259
00:09:40,668 --> 00:09:41,411
The ball is in.

260
00:09:41,803 --> 00:09:42,813
Hit it.

261
00:09:43,037 --> 00:09:44,414
Seung Ju pushes the ball over the net.

262
00:09:44,839 --> 00:09:46,049
It's blocked.

263
00:09:47,037 --> 00:09:48,191
(Free ball for Suwon)

264
00:09:48,192 --> 00:09:49,302
Quick attack!

265
00:09:50,211 --> 00:09:52,055
Quick attack!

266
00:09:52,613 --> 00:09:55,859
(It isn't a quick attack?)

267
00:09:56,879 --> 00:09:59,224
(They got us!)

268
00:09:59,887 --> 00:10:01,331
(Hyeon Ju's spike)

269
00:10:03,550 --> 00:10:05,126
(A perfect dig)

270
00:10:05,127 --> 00:10:06,204
A good dig again!

271
00:10:07,094 --> 00:10:08,071
(Dropping)

272
00:10:08,729 --> 00:10:09,906
(But it's a clean kill.)

273
00:10:09,913 --> 00:10:11,283
- They scored a point.
- That was clean.

274
00:10:11,533 --> 00:10:12,476
- Suwon!
- Let's go!

275
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:15,446
Thanks to Hyeon Ju's performance,
Suwon Special City takes the momentum.

276
00:10:15,446 --> 00:10:17,347
(Third set, Suwon Special City 4
: Wonder Dogs 3)

277
00:10:17,572 --> 00:10:19,507
- You saved it nicely, though.
- Just one. Right away.

278
00:10:19,507 --> 00:10:20,718
Let's just go for it immediately.

279
00:10:21,142 --> 00:10:23,020
Let's score a point right away.

280
00:10:23,878 --> 00:10:26,023
- To the side, okay?
- Yes.

281
00:10:27,159 --> 00:10:28,136
Seung Ju, look at this.

282
00:10:28,493 --> 00:10:30,538
Target in between.

283
00:10:31,252 --> 00:10:32,497
Get it? Target in between.

284
00:10:32,521 --> 00:10:35,766
The Wonder Dogs
really need to step up again.

285
00:10:35,766 --> 00:10:37,868
They need to regain their rhythm now.

286
00:10:38,459 --> 00:10:39,469
In 1, 2!

287
00:10:40,428 --> 00:10:42,330
- Good!
- What a precise reception.

288
00:10:42,330 --> 00:10:43,541
(Tossing accurately in between)

289
00:10:43,843 --> 00:10:45,487
(And Seung Ju is ready to attack!)

290
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:47,211
That's it!

291
00:10:48,569 --> 00:10:50,438
(Spike in between the defenders)

292
00:10:50,438 --> 00:10:52,182
- Seung Ju!
- That was nice.

293
00:10:52,182 --> 00:10:56,444
Seung Ju shifts the team's momentum
whenever it's needed.

294
00:10:57,111 --> 00:10:58,221
Good.

295
00:11:00,281 --> 00:11:01,992
Goodness!

296
00:11:03,817 --> 00:11:06,653
(Riding the momentum, Captain Pyo serves.)

297
00:11:09,156 --> 00:11:10,480
Go! Hit it!

298
00:11:10,481 --> 00:11:11,492
(Sudden quick attack)

299
00:11:11,492 --> 00:11:12,269
Set it!

300
00:11:13,961 --> 00:11:15,238
Go!

301
00:11:15,238 --> 00:11:17,006
(The Wonder Dogs' attack chance)

302
00:11:17,765 --> 00:11:21,779
(Enkhsoyol is jumping!)

303
00:11:23,971 --> 00:11:26,249
(Will she aim in between again?)

304
00:11:28,042 --> 00:11:29,119
Good. Let's go.

305
00:11:29,768 --> 00:11:33,781
The straight attack lands along the line.

306
00:11:34,348 --> 00:11:37,039
Enkhsoyol is improving really fast.

307
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,636
Indeed. As we can see,

308
00:11:38,637 --> 00:11:41,355
she is showing various attack options.

309
00:11:41,355 --> 00:11:42,933
Earlier, she went
for a deep cross-court attack,

310
00:11:42,933 --> 00:11:46,270
and just now, she hit a straight low shot,

311
00:11:46,270 --> 00:11:48,195
and she's also mixing in some feints.

312
00:11:48,195 --> 00:11:49,673
I hope this serve can...

313
00:11:49,673 --> 00:11:52,309
decide their victory.

314
00:11:52,309 --> 00:11:53,810
She has to show something here.

315
00:11:54,335 --> 00:11:56,018
(Instructing the target zone)

316
00:11:56,203 --> 00:11:57,847
(The target zone)

317
00:11:58,005 --> 00:11:59,983
(Got it!)

318
00:12:00,942 --> 00:12:02,353
- More!
- Out!

319
00:12:03,911 --> 00:12:04,988
- More!
- Out!

320
00:12:05,379 --> 00:12:06,790
(In)

321
00:12:07,315 --> 00:12:09,449
(A decisive point)

322
00:12:09,449 --> 00:12:12,395
She adds another point
as her team takes the lead!

323
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,530
More.

324
00:12:13,654 --> 00:12:18,635
(They were helpless
before the targeted attack.)

325
00:12:18,893 --> 00:12:21,138
(Nice serve!)

326
00:12:21,462 --> 00:12:23,240
(The Wonder Dogs are on a roll.)

327
00:12:23,798 --> 00:12:24,975
The reception is shaky.

328
00:12:27,902 --> 00:12:29,479
It's a free ball for Suwon Special City.

329
00:12:31,277 --> 00:12:32,921
(Slide attack)

330
00:12:33,741 --> 00:12:34,985
Quick attack.

331
00:12:35,376 --> 00:12:36,553
It's a touch-out.

332
00:12:37,111 --> 00:12:38,622
They need to stay focused.

333
00:12:38,622 --> 00:12:40,791
(Halting the team's momentum)

334
00:12:41,297 --> 00:12:44,009
(Suwon Special City is
sticking close persistently.)

335
00:12:44,418 --> 00:12:48,064
(They're never an easy opponent.)

336
00:12:48,389 --> 00:12:49,966
The game resumes with Na Hee's serve.

337
00:12:49,966 --> 00:12:51,768
(Third set, Suwon Special City 8
: Wonder Dogs 8)

338
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:53,837
Mine.

339
00:12:55,329 --> 00:12:56,306
She moves down and sets the ball.

340
00:12:56,464 --> 00:12:57,307
And a back-row attack.

341
00:12:59,918 --> 00:13:02,730
(Will it be a blocker touch-out again?)

342
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:04,614
(Song Hee's coverage)

343
00:13:05,339 --> 00:13:08,048
(They managed to save the ball,)

344
00:13:08,536 --> 00:13:10,114
(and Enkhsoyol finishes the play.)

345
00:13:10,114 --> 00:13:12,655
Enkhsoyol smashes it!

346
00:13:13,247 --> 00:13:15,516
(A point from a blocker touch-out)

347
00:13:15,516 --> 00:13:17,661
- Nice!
- They take the lead back.

348
00:13:18,819 --> 00:13:21,297
(Proud)

349
00:13:21,695 --> 00:13:26,075
(An attack struck at the perfect spot)

350
00:13:26,446 --> 00:13:28,457
(His mouth is dry.)

351
00:13:28,745 --> 00:13:30,600
(A fierce battle for a single point)

352
00:13:32,198 --> 00:13:33,041
Yeon Jae.

353
00:13:33,041 --> 00:13:34,876
(Yeon Jae's attack failed.)

354
00:13:35,801 --> 00:13:36,678
Once again.

355
00:13:37,069 --> 00:13:37,946
It's blocked!

356
00:13:37,946 --> 00:13:39,147
(The follow-up attack failed too.)

357
00:13:39,406 --> 00:13:40,549
(Good job.)

358
00:13:41,674 --> 00:13:44,219
It's a free ball.
The buildup starts from Myoung Hwa!

359
00:13:45,311 --> 00:13:46,488
Toward the right back row!

360
00:13:46,879 --> 00:13:50,516
The A route is closed!

361
00:13:50,517 --> 00:13:51,817
(A free ball again)

362
00:13:51,817 --> 00:13:52,785
Where will the ball head this time?

363
00:13:52,785 --> 00:13:54,820
(Where will Sol's ball go?)

364
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:56,564
Enkhsoyol's soft tip!

365
00:13:57,851 --> 00:13:59,362
The ball is back to the Wonder Dogs.

366
00:13:59,892 --> 00:14:02,170
(To Enkhsoyol again!)

367
00:14:03,029 --> 00:14:05,865
A smash by Enkhsoyol!

368
00:14:05,865 --> 00:14:07,843
(Enkhsoyol scored once again.)

369
00:14:09,301 --> 00:14:10,378
(The game continues.)

370
00:14:10,970 --> 00:14:11,837
A quick attack.

371
00:14:11,837 --> 00:14:13,672
(Enkhsoyol's straight attack)

372
00:14:13,672 --> 00:14:14,549
- Hit it.
- Go!

373
00:14:15,107 --> 00:14:16,384
A back-row attack by Hyeon Ju.

374
00:14:16,536 --> 00:14:18,735
(They have another attack chance.)

375
00:14:19,034 --> 00:14:21,646
(If the straight attack is blocked...)

376
00:14:22,681 --> 00:14:25,493
The feint attack worked!

377
00:14:25,885 --> 00:14:27,196
Good job!

378
00:14:28,454 --> 00:14:30,799
(In the following rally)

379
00:14:32,792 --> 00:14:36,405
- There she goes!
- A soft push over the net by Enkhsoyol!

380
00:14:36,728 --> 00:14:39,154
It's Enkhsoyol!

381
00:14:39,154 --> 00:14:39,931
Good.

382
00:14:39,932 --> 00:14:41,176
(Third set, Suwon Special City 10
: Wonder Dogs 13)

383
00:14:41,394 --> 00:14:44,173
Enkhsoyol is now skillfully varying
the intensity of her attacks.

384
00:14:44,637 --> 00:14:45,339
Serve!

385
00:14:45,339 --> 00:14:46,983
(She isn't just good at attacking.)

386
00:14:47,573 --> 00:14:48,474
(Enkhsoyol's power serve...)
What a power serve.

387
00:14:49,875 --> 00:14:50,910
The reception is shaky.

388
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:52,588
(shakes the opponents.)

389
00:14:53,145 --> 00:14:54,889
The ball hits the net.

390
00:14:55,648 --> 00:14:59,027
- All this starts from a strong serve.
- Right.

391
00:14:59,485 --> 00:15:00,786
Enkhsoyol. Here.

392
00:15:01,554 --> 00:15:02,397
Okay!

393
00:15:05,845 --> 00:15:07,393
(Enkhsoyol's serve...)

394
00:15:07,393 --> 00:15:08,904
Enkhsoyol showed a nice serve.

395
00:15:11,318 --> 00:15:12,198
(leads to errors from the opponents.)

396
00:15:12,198 --> 00:15:13,579
With their reception faltering,

397
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,187
Suwon Special City committed
another mistake.

398
00:15:15,434 --> 00:15:18,346
In the end,
the powerful serve results in a point.

399
00:15:19,249 --> 00:15:21,750
(Third set, Suwon Special City 12
: Wonder Dogs 19)

400
00:15:22,467 --> 00:15:24,365
(They are completely on a roll right now.)

401
00:15:24,365 --> 00:15:25,174
Let's change now.

402
00:15:26,212 --> 00:15:28,214
I can't believe
what the Wonder Dogs are about to do.

403
00:15:28,214 --> 00:15:29,024
Same here.

404
00:15:29,024 --> 00:15:30,893
They're the setter
while they are in good form.

405
00:15:30,893 --> 00:15:32,715
(From Sol to Young In)

406
00:15:32,741 --> 00:15:34,990
Now, Jin and Young In are on the court.

407
00:15:37,066 --> 00:15:40,312
It somehow feels really weird.

408
00:15:41,135 --> 00:15:44,281
I really want to show
how much I've improved here.

409
00:15:45,673 --> 00:15:48,852
I want them to feel my absence.

410
00:15:49,977 --> 00:15:51,922
I really want to play well.

411
00:15:52,413 --> 00:15:54,358
Jin and Young In are on the court now.

412
00:15:54,381 --> 00:15:56,159
This might become a new strategy.

413
00:15:56,159 --> 00:15:58,185
(Could this substitution be
the key to victory?)

414
00:15:58,185 --> 00:15:59,229
Jin.

415
00:16:01,322 --> 00:16:03,223
Focus on using the middles
and pipe attacks frequently.

416
00:16:03,223 --> 00:16:04,634
Those will work for sure.

417
00:16:04,634 --> 00:16:07,200
(Instructing the middle attack,
which she's been emphasizing)

418
00:16:08,629 --> 00:16:09,863
(Due to the continued use
of the left-side attack,)

419
00:16:09,863 --> 00:16:12,108
That side keeps getting overloaded.

420
00:16:12,853 --> 00:16:16,491
(the left-side player quickly tired.)

421
00:16:17,106 --> 00:16:21,193
(She has continuously called for attacks
from the middle and the right.)

422
00:16:22,401 --> 00:16:25,881
(Got it.)

423
00:16:26,416 --> 00:16:29,094
(Myoung Hwa's serve)

424
00:16:29,283 --> 00:16:30,327
Okay!

425
00:16:31,785 --> 00:16:33,096
A good toss!

426
00:16:34,688 --> 00:16:35,832
Myoung Hwa digs it!

427
00:16:36,419 --> 00:16:37,984
(Is the ball set...)

428
00:16:37,984 --> 00:16:39,619
(to the left again?)

429
00:16:39,644 --> 00:16:40,862
Seung Ju!

430
00:16:40,863 --> 00:16:41,654
(It's blocked!)

431
00:16:41,654 --> 00:16:43,232
But it's blocked.

432
00:16:44,057 --> 00:16:46,035
- I'm sorry.
- My bad.

433
00:16:46,259 --> 00:16:47,203
Let's get it started right away.

434
00:16:48,444 --> 00:16:49,245
(So, no more left.)

435
00:16:49,246 --> 00:16:50,657
I shouldn't hit it that way.

436
00:16:51,597 --> 00:16:54,210
- Jin, do it as I said.
- Okay.

437
00:16:55,001 --> 00:16:56,512
- Play as I instructed.
- Okay.

438
00:16:56,512 --> 00:16:57,546
(Emphasizing the middle attack)

439
00:16:58,214 --> 00:16:59,291
The score is 19 to 13.

440
00:17:01,753 --> 00:17:02,930
Seung Ju, it's this!

441
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:03,965
Serve!

442
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:06,510
(Copy that!)

443
00:17:06,928 --> 00:17:08,259
(A serve by Ye Dam)

444
00:17:08,259 --> 00:17:09,103
Serve!

445
00:17:10,261 --> 00:17:10,972
Mine.

446
00:17:10,972 --> 00:17:12,573
Seung Ju receives it on a slide.

447
00:17:12,741 --> 00:17:15,220
(A rapid slide attack)

448
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,944
Aiming for the back row! It's Na Hee.

449
00:17:16,944 --> 00:17:17,711
Get it!
Cover the area!

450
00:17:18,770 --> 00:17:20,548
- She sets the ball!
- Dink it!

451
00:17:20,939 --> 00:17:22,207
She sent the ball over the net.

452
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,351
Enkhsoyol saves it!

453
00:17:23,351 --> 00:17:25,310
Toss it to her now!

454
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:26,354
Now!

455
00:17:26,678 --> 00:17:28,122
(But the ball goes to Seung Ju.)

456
00:17:28,146 --> 00:17:29,056
Shoot.

457
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:30,157
Seung Ju's soft tip!

458
00:17:30,582 --> 00:17:32,660
Set it to her again, like I said!

459
00:17:33,017 --> 00:17:33,794
Ye Dam.

460
00:17:34,519 --> 00:17:35,999
(Hyeon Ju's counterattack)

461
00:17:36,265 --> 00:17:38,076
(And Seung Ju is alone at the net.)

462
00:17:38,690 --> 00:17:40,554
(Seung Ju, you remember it, right?)

463
00:17:40,792 --> 00:17:41,635
Mine.

464
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:43,720
(Absolutely!)

465
00:17:44,229 --> 00:17:47,308
Seung Ju with the block!

466
00:17:47,308 --> 00:17:48,709
(General Pyo is reliable even on her own.)

467
00:17:48,709 --> 00:17:50,377
Seung Ju is very reliable.

468
00:17:50,969 --> 00:17:51,879
Jin.

469
00:17:52,904 --> 00:17:54,882
What did I tell you to do
if it doesn't result in a point?

470
00:17:55,495 --> 00:17:56,372
I have to set it again.

471
00:17:56,914 --> 00:17:58,625
I told you to set it to her again!

472
00:17:59,778 --> 00:18:01,155
Okay. I'm sorry.

473
00:18:03,678 --> 00:18:06,311
(The Wonder Dogs' serve again)

474
00:18:07,152 --> 00:18:07,995
Mine.

475
00:18:07,996 --> 00:18:09,817
(A high, floating free ball)

476
00:18:10,156 --> 00:18:13,384
(A powerful spike without missing)

477
00:18:13,825 --> 00:18:14,602
Spike!

478
00:18:14,826 --> 00:18:15,603
Young In!

479
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,870
Hyeon Ju digs!

480
00:18:18,292 --> 00:18:20,337
(Yuni's soft tip)

481
00:18:21,499 --> 00:18:22,242
Mine!

482
00:18:22,567 --> 00:18:24,044
Jin made a great set!

483
00:18:24,045 --> 00:18:25,455
Step in!

484
00:18:25,455 --> 00:18:26,547
(And the ball goes to Seung Ju.)

485
00:18:26,971 --> 00:18:29,917
Seung Ju's point from a feint
in Zone Three!

486
00:18:30,542 --> 00:18:33,087
Nice feint!

487
00:18:33,378 --> 00:18:35,424
(Seung Ju pulled it off again!)

488
00:18:35,424 --> 00:18:36,724
The score is 21 to 13.

489
00:18:38,011 --> 00:18:40,173
(Instructing a targeted serve)

490
00:18:40,479 --> 00:18:42,524
(Target zone)

491
00:18:43,321 --> 00:18:44,331
A serve by Jin.

492
00:18:45,297 --> 00:18:46,307
Darn it.

493
00:18:47,525 --> 00:18:49,103
(The serve goes astray.)

494
00:18:49,328 --> 00:18:50,338
Hey!

495
00:18:51,263 --> 00:18:52,106
Hyo Rim.
Get it!

496
00:18:53,131 --> 00:18:53,785
Hit it!

497
00:18:53,785 --> 00:18:55,596
(Hyeon Ju jumps into the air again.)

498
00:18:57,188 --> 00:19:00,201
Hyeon Ju goes
for cross-court attacks a lot.

499
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,299
(And she really executed
a cross-court attack.)

500
00:19:02,935 --> 00:19:05,747
(They've defended it well so far.)

501
00:19:06,338 --> 00:19:08,049
(How about this time?)

502
00:19:09,078 --> 00:19:10,698
(Breaking through)

503
00:19:10,817 --> 00:19:11,560
Hit it!

504
00:19:13,078 --> 00:19:13,855
Good!

505
00:19:14,747 --> 00:19:16,447
(A failed dig)

506
00:19:16,782 --> 00:19:17,525
Jin!

507
00:19:18,584 --> 00:19:20,240
- Where should you position yourself?
- Here.

508
00:19:28,249 --> 00:19:30,882
(Coach Kim is frustrated
by their continuous mistakes.)

509
00:19:31,988 --> 00:19:33,188
Where is she going?

510
00:19:33,949 --> 00:19:35,482
(Speechless)

511
00:19:35,882 --> 00:19:37,282
It's 14 to 22.

512
00:19:37,949 --> 00:19:39,916
Back Chae Rim goes in as well.

513
00:19:40,682 --> 00:19:44,282
Now, all three players
who were in Suwon Special City...

514
00:19:44,282 --> 00:19:46,182
- are on the court for the first time.
- You're right.

515
00:19:47,216 --> 00:19:49,016
(It's time to give back...)

516
00:19:49,682 --> 00:19:53,149
(what they got from their former team.)

517
00:19:55,249 --> 00:19:56,582
(They shook their reception!)

518
00:19:57,216 --> 00:19:58,316
It's coming over!

519
00:19:59,016 --> 00:20:00,482
(A free ball heads to them.)

520
00:20:03,216 --> 00:20:07,016
Kim Na Hee's direct attack!

521
00:20:07,949 --> 00:20:11,016
The former players from Suwon Special City
were in perfect sync.

522
00:20:11,316 --> 00:20:13,682
- Nice serve, Chae Rim!
- Nice!

523
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,716
(Chae Rim serves again.)

524
00:20:22,316 --> 00:20:23,816
(Kim Bo Been runs.)

525
00:20:23,982 --> 00:20:25,349
(Attacking the open spot)

526
00:20:27,649 --> 00:20:29,216
- Koo Hye In digs!
- Great!

527
00:20:29,216 --> 00:20:30,282
Back toss.

528
00:20:30,282 --> 00:20:31,782
Yoon Young In!

529
00:20:33,382 --> 00:20:35,882
(Their tip comes next.)

530
00:20:36,182 --> 00:20:37,916
Tips come first to the players here.

531
00:20:38,316 --> 00:20:40,616
Those in zone 1 should prioritize
watching tip attacks.

532
00:20:41,516 --> 00:20:43,216
(Zone 1)

533
00:20:46,182 --> 00:20:47,182
Tip!

534
00:20:47,182 --> 00:20:48,582
(They fail to defend.)

535
00:20:50,616 --> 00:20:51,616
Jin!

536
00:20:53,916 --> 00:20:55,016
Jin!

537
00:20:56,349 --> 00:20:58,794
Jin!

538
00:21:00,661 --> 00:21:02,161
Concentrate!

539
00:21:05,916 --> 00:21:06,916
Timeout.

540
00:21:06,916 --> 00:21:08,349
(She requests a timeout.)

541
00:21:09,382 --> 00:21:10,749
She immediately calls a timeout.

542
00:21:11,649 --> 00:21:13,616
(The atmosphere turns tense at once.)

543
00:21:16,349 --> 00:21:17,682
Where did I tell you to watch?

544
00:21:20,116 --> 00:21:22,282
How many times is this?
Where should you watch when it's Hyeon Ju?

545
00:21:22,649 --> 00:21:24,582
Cross-court.

546
00:21:25,316 --> 00:21:26,882
I told you to stay there.
You missed so many!

547
00:21:26,882 --> 00:21:28,016
(They missed cross-court spikes.)

548
00:21:28,949 --> 00:21:30,382
What did I tell you about the high ball?

549
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:33,182
How should you defend in zone 1
when the ball is high?

550
00:21:34,216 --> 00:21:35,216
Defend a tip.

551
00:21:36,882 --> 00:21:38,082
You missed a lot!

552
00:21:39,049 --> 00:21:42,682
Coach Kim is really strict
in what they have trained.

553
00:21:42,682 --> 00:21:43,716
She is.

554
00:21:43,716 --> 00:21:45,582
(Even if they score,)

555
00:21:46,216 --> 00:21:49,282
(she scolds them
when they didn't play as instructed.)

556
00:21:52,416 --> 00:21:55,749
(The process matters more than the score.)

557
00:21:55,982 --> 00:22:00,216
Even if they get a point
but don't play as planned,

558
00:22:00,349 --> 00:22:02,716
she points that out clearly.

559
00:22:03,449 --> 00:22:06,016
(Coach Kim reminds the players
of how they should play.)

560
00:22:06,582 --> 00:22:08,882
- Follow the plan.
- Focus.

561
00:22:08,882 --> 00:22:11,449
- Stick to our strategy.
- Jin.

562
00:22:11,616 --> 00:22:13,816
Don't give up. You must keep going.

563
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:17,349
Coach got upset with us
because we couldn't follow our plan.

564
00:22:17,349 --> 00:22:18,716
Remember your roles.

565
00:22:18,749 --> 00:22:20,716
Take her words positively.

566
00:22:20,849 --> 00:22:22,082
Let's see this through!

567
00:22:22,149 --> 00:22:24,816
Players are comforting her
despite the challenge.

568
00:22:25,882 --> 00:22:26,982
Let's go!

569
00:22:29,049 --> 00:22:30,182
It's okay. Get ready.

570
00:22:30,516 --> 00:22:32,916
Lee Jin wanted to do her best.

571
00:22:32,916 --> 00:22:33,916
Enkhsoyol.

572
00:22:43,582 --> 00:22:45,116
I shouldn't have done that.

573
00:22:47,349 --> 00:22:50,482
I joined the team to do better,
but I wasn't sure if I was doing it right.

574
00:22:50,649 --> 00:22:54,482
And I was lost in that thought.

575
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,549
I see the whole thing outside.

576
00:22:56,916 --> 00:22:59,616
But when I'm in, I get confused.

577
00:23:00,149 --> 00:23:01,749
So I just can't get it right.

578
00:23:01,895 --> 00:23:04,428
I also think too much,
and I end up ruining.

579
00:23:06,282 --> 00:23:09,549
Still, it became my turning point.

580
00:23:10,183 --> 00:23:12,249
"I can't let myself get scolded."

581
00:23:12,416 --> 00:23:14,216
That thought was stuck in my head.

582
00:23:14,982 --> 00:23:17,349
"I'll just cry it all out
and concentrate."

583
00:23:17,716 --> 00:23:19,616
(The setter is the key figure
on the court.)

584
00:23:19,749 --> 00:23:22,516
I guess I just played,
trusting my teammates.

585
00:23:24,082 --> 00:23:27,749
(For my teammates who believe in me)

586
00:23:28,116 --> 00:23:31,082
I wanted to finish the third set
no matter what.

587
00:23:34,049 --> 00:23:35,882
(The game is not over yet!)

588
00:23:35,882 --> 00:23:37,016
Here!

589
00:23:38,949 --> 00:23:40,782
(The ball distracts the blocker.)

590
00:23:40,782 --> 00:23:41,982
Okay!

591
00:23:42,316 --> 00:23:43,816
Lee Jin tossed it well.

592
00:23:46,849 --> 00:23:48,282
(Young In's spike)

593
00:23:48,782 --> 00:23:50,016
Yoon Young In!

594
00:23:50,016 --> 00:23:51,395
(A refreshing combination attack)

595
00:23:51,396 --> 00:23:52,696
That's it!

596
00:23:53,362 --> 00:23:54,896
All right. Jin is back.

597
00:23:54,896 --> 00:23:56,696
- Nice toss!
- Nice toss!

598
00:23:57,296 --> 00:23:58,429
That's how you do it.

599
00:23:58,429 --> 00:24:01,162
You just need to show your skill
right on the court.

600
00:24:02,529 --> 00:24:04,929
It's now the Wonder Dogs' match point.

601
00:24:05,829 --> 00:24:07,787
(If they score here,)

602
00:24:08,251 --> 00:24:10,151
(it'll be a perfect shutout victory.)

603
00:24:10,514 --> 00:24:12,409
(With just one point left,
how will it turn out?)

604
00:24:12,760 --> 00:24:14,393
(The Wonder Dogs' match point)

605
00:24:15,114 --> 00:24:16,114
Koo Hye In.

606
00:24:16,114 --> 00:24:17,681
(It's their chance!)

607
00:24:18,114 --> 00:24:20,214
(Attack of Run Myoung Hwa)

608
00:24:24,014 --> 00:24:27,126
Lee Jin and Moon Myoung Hwa!

609
00:24:27,126 --> 00:24:29,647
(Myoung Hwa wraps up the game.)

610
00:24:32,581 --> 00:24:33,747
(Roaring)

611
00:24:34,781 --> 00:24:36,081
(Cheering)

612
00:24:36,714 --> 00:24:37,981
Great work.

613
00:24:38,281 --> 00:24:39,347
(Tapping)

614
00:24:41,081 --> 00:24:42,814
It's 25 to 16!

615
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:46,114
The Wonder Dogs win the match
against Suwon Special City...

616
00:24:46,281 --> 00:24:50,347
with the perfect score of three to zero,
marking a consecutive victory.

617
00:24:50,947 --> 00:24:52,314
I can't believe this!

618
00:24:52,314 --> 00:24:57,147
The whole team played as one,
with no one left out.

619
00:24:57,581 --> 00:25:00,314
(Wonder Dogs 3: Suwon Special City 0)

620
00:25:00,314 --> 00:25:02,281
Great job!

621
00:25:02,281 --> 00:25:05,781
The journey from tryout
to training sessions was...

622
00:25:05,914 --> 00:25:07,981
really difficult.

623
00:25:08,381 --> 00:25:10,114
I keep improving as well.

624
00:25:10,114 --> 00:25:12,881
It's like I'm growing together
with my players.

625
00:25:13,714 --> 00:25:17,447
Just like players getting better,

626
00:25:17,514 --> 00:25:23,081
I can say I'm also growing
to be a better coach and a leader.

627
00:25:23,414 --> 00:25:25,147
I'm really grateful for my players.

628
00:25:26,581 --> 00:25:30,281
(Meanwhile, after the match)

629
00:25:30,627 --> 00:25:31,993
It still bothered me.

630
00:25:32,367 --> 00:25:37,534
Suwon Special City could have shown
everything they got...

631
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:40,574
before they lost, nevertheless.

632
00:25:40,853 --> 00:25:43,520
That's why I was worried about them.

633
00:25:44,714 --> 00:25:47,861
Coach Kang said, "You did great,"
and "Well done" to us.

634
00:25:48,153 --> 00:25:52,639
He told us we improved a lot.

635
00:25:52,850 --> 00:25:55,450
And he advised us
to take care of ourselves...

636
00:25:55,450 --> 00:25:57,250
while we were on the team.

637
00:25:57,250 --> 00:26:00,084
He kept showing concern before he left.

638
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:04,184
(A few days ago,
when Coach Kang sneaked up)

639
00:26:04,184 --> 00:26:06,556
- Hello?
- Coach, did you make it safely?

640
00:26:06,983 --> 00:26:08,783
- Yes. I'm on my way.
- Really?

641
00:26:09,317 --> 00:26:11,950
I'm sorry that I couldn't come
to you for a greeting.

642
00:26:11,950 --> 00:26:12,950
It's okay.

643
00:26:13,184 --> 00:26:15,917
I just came to see Na Hee out of concern.

644
00:26:17,179 --> 00:26:19,018
(Due to a minor injury,)

645
00:26:19,277 --> 00:26:21,110
(Na Hee couldn't play during the match
with Shujitsu High School.)

646
00:26:22,050 --> 00:26:24,893
Seeing how she was doing
made me relieved to go.

647
00:26:26,214 --> 00:26:28,514
(Coach Kang actually came
to look after the players.)

648
00:26:29,414 --> 00:26:32,814
(Behind the players who took
a step forward to improve,)

649
00:26:34,214 --> 00:26:39,581
(there was always a head coach
watching them from afar.)

650
00:26:40,781 --> 00:26:42,948
(The team's first consecutive win
since their foundation)

651
00:26:43,381 --> 00:26:45,648
- We made it.
- I know, right?

652
00:26:47,528 --> 00:26:48,528
This guy is alive.

653
00:26:51,748 --> 00:26:53,881
We kept the pieces safe.

654
00:26:59,248 --> 00:27:01,248
(Nervous for no reason)

655
00:27:02,181 --> 00:27:03,181
Gifts for you.

656
00:27:03,181 --> 00:27:05,081
(Ta-da! It's a surprise gift.)

657
00:27:05,714 --> 00:27:07,814
(In awe)

658
00:27:07,814 --> 00:27:09,648
I'm giving you these because you won.

659
00:27:11,248 --> 00:27:13,248
- It's good for your skin. Try it.
- Thank you.

660
00:27:14,148 --> 00:27:15,414
Think of your skin.

661
00:27:17,114 --> 00:27:20,014
(The rookie coach may not think
of losing,)

662
00:27:21,081 --> 00:27:24,014
(but she thinks of her skin greatly.)

663
00:27:24,914 --> 00:27:28,281
(Always listen
to Coach Kim's instruction!)

664
00:27:28,914 --> 00:27:31,300
(Hitting her skin relentlessly)

665
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:32,600
This sticks well.

666
00:27:33,034 --> 00:27:34,834
Yes. No wonder Coach likes it.

667
00:27:34,834 --> 00:27:36,034
(Skins exhausted by receptions
and blocks?)

668
00:27:36,034 --> 00:27:37,034
This is really good.

669
00:27:37,034 --> 00:27:38,367
(They got better thanks to Coach Kim!)

670
00:27:39,234 --> 00:27:41,467
I'll announce your next opponent.

671
00:27:43,301 --> 00:27:46,907
(They currently have three wins
and three defeats.)

672
00:27:47,606 --> 00:27:51,140
(With just one more victory,)

673
00:27:52,300 --> 00:27:55,333
(the team will survive!)

674
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:58,207
(Their next opponent,
who will set their fate is...)

675
00:27:58,226 --> 00:28:01,826
(The Red Sparks)

676
00:28:02,406 --> 00:28:05,673
(It's the pro team again.)

677
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:08,843
Hello.

678
00:28:09,468 --> 00:28:12,881
I'm Ko Hee Jin, coach of the Red Sparks.
Nice to meet you.

679
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:17,185
(What do you think about Coach Kim?)

680
00:28:19,431 --> 00:28:23,911
Yeon Koung has the best qualities
to be a great coach.

681
00:28:25,003 --> 00:28:25,980
Here's why.

682
00:28:26,004 --> 00:28:27,915
She has unique leadership skills.

683
00:28:27,939 --> 00:28:31,419
With that, she knows
how to bring her team together.

684
00:28:32,277 --> 00:28:36,457
That's not something just anyone can do.

685
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:39,093
I think that's her biggest strength.

686
00:28:41,953 --> 00:28:44,365
(What kind of player was Seung Ju?)

687
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:47,768
It's quite threatening to have Seung Ju...

688
00:28:47,792 --> 00:28:49,670
on the Wonder Dogs, playing against us.

689
00:28:50,804 --> 00:28:52,749
She was a great leader,

690
00:28:52,772 --> 00:28:56,752
and that's how we became finalists
for the first time in 13 years.

691
00:28:56,776 --> 00:28:58,654
She was like a lucky charm.

692
00:28:58,812 --> 00:28:59,989
I'm really grateful to her.

693
00:29:02,149 --> 00:29:04,794
(He takes a look
at the Wonder Dogs' lineup.)

694
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:09,432
Well, based on the lineup...

695
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:13,569
I think it's a bit too weak...

696
00:29:13,727 --> 00:29:15,738
for Yeon Koung to bring out her A-game.

697
00:29:23,103 --> 00:29:25,214
It takes good ingredients...

698
00:29:25,479 --> 00:29:27,090
to make a great dish.

699
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:29,778
I believe in my players.

700
00:29:29,809 --> 00:29:31,687
My job will probably just be
applauding in the back.

701
00:29:33,046 --> 00:29:34,390
(Laughing)

702
00:29:42,622 --> 00:29:44,900
(Share your thoughts with us
before the match against the Red Sparks.)

703
00:29:44,925 --> 00:29:50,306
I think this is the strongest team we've
faced so far.

704
00:29:50,363 --> 00:29:51,640
So...

705
00:29:52,699 --> 00:29:54,110
it's kind of exciting.

706
00:29:54,768 --> 00:29:56,646
I can't wait.

707
00:29:56,670 --> 00:29:58,848
I feel that way
because I can really see...

708
00:29:58,939 --> 00:30:01,651
how much our players have grown.

709
00:30:01,976 --> 00:30:04,687
I'm curious to see how much...

710
00:30:05,078 --> 00:30:08,158
they've improved and progressed.

711
00:30:08,182 --> 00:30:10,660
As their coach,
I'm truly looking forward to it.

712
00:30:11,685 --> 00:30:14,163
(A few days later)

713
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:15,464
How are you all today?

714
00:30:16,223 --> 00:30:17,567
Are you okay? Are you ready?

715
00:30:18,124 --> 00:30:19,568
By the way, we look kind of shabby today.

716
00:30:19,593 --> 00:30:21,404
We only have 2, 4, 6, 8...

717
00:30:21,862 --> 00:30:24,073
only 11 players today.

718
00:30:24,631 --> 00:30:26,609
We look a bit pathetic.

719
00:30:27,267 --> 00:30:31,047
(The court used to be
crowded with players.)

720
00:30:31,404 --> 00:30:35,617
(All 14 players used to train together.)

721
00:30:35,775 --> 00:30:37,886
(After the match
against Suwon Special City)

722
00:30:38,812 --> 00:30:39,889
I'll get going.

723
00:30:40,013 --> 00:30:42,291
I'll join you after some hard training.

724
00:30:42,949 --> 00:30:44,026
Don't get hurt.

725
00:30:44,184 --> 00:30:46,829
Bye! See you soon!

726
00:30:46,853 --> 00:30:49,180
(Back Chae Rim)

727
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:50,242
(Yoon Young In)

728
00:30:50,242 --> 00:30:53,003
(A few players left the team temporarily.)

729
00:30:54,628 --> 00:30:56,272
We don't have as many players
as we used to.

730
00:30:56,296 --> 00:30:59,041
(Na Hee, Chae Rim, and Young In are
Suwon Special City players.)

731
00:30:59,499 --> 00:31:03,345
(Due to an overseas match,)

732
00:31:03,603 --> 00:31:06,248
(the three players are absent.)

733
00:31:06,272 --> 00:31:07,816
The members are the same, right?

734
00:31:07,841 --> 00:31:10,453
You remember these faces.

735
00:31:11,344 --> 00:31:16,659
(The three absent players have
always been starting members.)

736
00:31:17,317 --> 00:31:20,463
Losing three players in Wonder Dogs is...

737
00:31:20,487 --> 00:31:21,698
a huge loss.

738
00:31:21,823 --> 00:31:26,769
We have no choice but to play
with the members we have now.

739
00:31:27,294 --> 00:31:30,373
"We might lose. We have no substitutes.
This is a big deal."

740
00:31:30,397 --> 00:31:32,075
I got anxious.

741
00:31:33,033 --> 00:31:36,179
(And to make it worse,
their next opponent is...)

742
00:31:36,536 --> 00:31:40,749
(a pro team.)

743
00:31:41,740 --> 00:31:43,918
(Wonder Dogs...)

744
00:31:43,943 --> 00:31:49,258
(lost their first match
to a pro team as well.)

745
00:31:49,282 --> 00:31:52,628
If we say we lost
because we didn't have those players,

746
00:31:52,652 --> 00:31:54,263
that's just an excuse.

747
00:31:54,387 --> 00:31:58,400
I'll take responsibility as a pro
and do my best.

748
00:31:58,725 --> 00:32:00,403
I don't think we'll struggle...

749
00:32:00,660 --> 00:32:04,873
just because we're down a few players.

750
00:32:04,998 --> 00:32:09,178
I'll do my best to support them.

751
00:32:09,869 --> 00:32:13,816
(How will the new coach face this crisis?)

752
00:32:14,107 --> 00:32:15,518
(Joining in)

753
00:32:16,242 --> 00:32:17,085
That's two points.

754
00:32:18,111 --> 00:32:19,055
My gosh.

755
00:32:19,879 --> 00:32:21,523
All warmed up, right?

756
00:32:21,548 --> 00:32:22,492
(Cracking)

757
00:32:23,516 --> 00:32:24,660
(Groaning)

758
00:32:24,852 --> 00:32:26,595
The net is too low.

759
00:32:26,619 --> 00:32:28,096
She's this much higher than the net.

760
00:32:28,555 --> 00:32:29,765
- In 1, 2, 3!
- In 1, 2, 3!

761
00:32:29,789 --> 00:32:31,700
(When you don't have enough players...)

762
00:32:31,791 --> 00:32:32,668
My ball.

763
00:32:33,226 --> 00:32:35,437
(The coach joins in on training!)

764
00:32:35,695 --> 00:32:36,639
(Screaming)

765
00:32:39,366 --> 00:32:40,743
You have to get it!

766
00:32:40,767 --> 00:32:42,678
(She fills in,
throwing her body into the play.)

767
00:32:42,902 --> 00:32:44,713
It's my job...

768
00:32:45,172 --> 00:32:46,915
to fill in those gaps.

769
00:32:47,507 --> 00:32:48,784
I'll have to make it happen, right?

770
00:32:50,243 --> 00:32:53,722
It reminded me of
when I was still an athlete.

771
00:32:54,114 --> 00:32:55,358
It was fun.

772
00:32:57,417 --> 00:32:59,362
Okay! We got two points!

773
00:32:59,385 --> 00:33:00,929
Two points!

774
00:33:03,415 --> 00:33:06,961
(The Emperor's hunt begins now.)

775
00:33:08,253 --> 00:33:09,897
- Coach!
- Hit it!

776
00:33:09,921 --> 00:33:11,799
(She's all warmed up!)

777
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:12,633
My ball!

778
00:33:13,191 --> 00:33:13,934
Hit it!

779
00:33:13,959 --> 00:33:14,936
(One rookie coach...)

780
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:16,139
(equals three players?)

781
00:33:16,163 --> 00:33:17,405
My ball!

782
00:33:17,863 --> 00:33:18,706
Move aside!

783
00:33:19,131 --> 00:33:19,908
No! Darn it!

784
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:23,094
I told you to move aside!

785
00:33:23,095 --> 00:33:24,545
(The Yeon Koung we know is back!)

786
00:33:26,571 --> 00:33:29,717
(Her competitiveness is unstoppable.)

787
00:33:29,741 --> 00:33:30,485
My ball.

788
00:33:30,642 --> 00:33:31,886
Okay!

789
00:33:31,910 --> 00:33:33,187
(You don't want to face her
as your opponent.)

790
00:33:33,211 --> 00:33:35,356
Spread!

791
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:39,961
(Volleyball is the easiest thing for me!)

792
00:33:40,619 --> 00:33:41,462
Save it!

793
00:33:42,754 --> 00:33:44,465
(She doesn't even need to jump.)

794
00:33:44,790 --> 00:33:46,735
(Oh, no.)

795
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:49,070
(Did you see that?)

796
00:33:49,227 --> 00:33:50,104
Nice.

797
00:33:50,362 --> 00:33:52,140
You're nothing, okay?

798
00:33:52,631 --> 00:33:53,341
Seriously.

799
00:33:53,465 --> 00:33:54,675
You think you can make a comeback?

800
00:33:55,334 --> 00:33:56,578
I don't feel half bad, honestly.

801
00:33:58,970 --> 00:34:00,915
(Jumping so lightly)

802
00:34:03,141 --> 00:34:03,818
Hurry!

803
00:34:03,818 --> 00:34:04,876
(Spikes from a world-class spiker)

804
00:34:04,876 --> 00:34:06,487
The quick one! That's it!

805
00:34:08,414 --> 00:34:10,124
To the center!

806
00:34:10,148 --> 00:34:12,827
Hey! I told you to set it to the center.

807
00:34:14,953 --> 00:34:16,130
That's it. Good.

808
00:34:16,154 --> 00:34:18,699
(Even the other coaches join
the practice.)

809
00:34:20,726 --> 00:34:22,304
You have to move.

810
00:34:22,461 --> 00:34:23,271
Up!

811
00:34:23,295 --> 00:34:24,472
Hey!

812
00:34:25,597 --> 00:34:26,374
Are you tired?

813
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:29,143
Today's training is too hard.
I can't move my shoulders.

814
00:34:30,135 --> 00:34:31,479
(The coaches aren't the only ones...)

815
00:34:31,637 --> 00:34:33,248
(sensing the crisis.)

816
00:34:33,338 --> 00:34:33,981
I think so.

817
00:34:35,941 --> 00:34:39,754
(Jeong Jong Il, Lee Sang Hwa,
and Park Ye Jin)

818
00:34:40,646 --> 00:34:45,827
(The treatment room is open
for the players all day.)

819
00:34:47,352 --> 00:34:50,798
How did you feel today after practice?

820
00:34:50,822 --> 00:34:52,623
It'd be great to share
our thoughts with each other.

821
00:34:52,624 --> 00:34:54,135
(Meditation Instructor Certification:
Lee Sang Hwa)

822
00:34:54,893 --> 00:34:58,539
(Healthy minds live in healthy bodies.)

823
00:34:59,665 --> 00:35:02,477
(And one day, while they were
in full preparation)

824
00:35:03,168 --> 00:35:03,945
Attention.

825
00:35:04,870 --> 00:35:06,114
As your manager,

826
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:07,949
I've only been ball retriever so far.

827
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:09,317
But today,

828
00:35:09,875 --> 00:35:11,552
I'll brief you on the Red Sparks.

829
00:35:12,810 --> 00:35:15,355
(That's right, Manager Boo...)

830
00:35:15,380 --> 00:35:18,326
(has been the biggest fan
of the Red Sparks for 20 years.)

831
00:35:18,350 --> 00:35:20,695
That's why I really didn't like him...

832
00:35:20,719 --> 00:35:21,930
when I was playing for the Pink Spiders.

833
00:35:22,988 --> 00:35:25,433
I like HOSHI from SEVENTEEN!
Let's go, HOSHI!

834
00:35:26,058 --> 00:35:28,970
(Come on.)

835
00:35:29,094 --> 00:35:32,407
After hearing the news
that we'd face the Red Sparks,

836
00:35:32,597 --> 00:35:35,042
as a 20-year fan of the team,

837
00:35:35,066 --> 00:35:37,645
I couldn't help but think...

838
00:35:37,669 --> 00:35:40,683
about their strengths and weaknesses,

839
00:35:40,707 --> 00:35:44,385
and how we can use them to our advantage.

840
00:35:44,710 --> 00:35:48,657
That's why I prepared today's presentation
as the team's strategist.

841
00:35:49,114 --> 00:35:53,027
Personally, I want you
to focus on this player.

842
00:35:53,652 --> 00:35:54,596
Shin Eun Ji.

843
00:35:54,620 --> 00:35:56,831
I think she's kind of a wild card.

844
00:35:56,855 --> 00:35:59,500
She's the best server in the whole league.

845
00:35:59,524 --> 00:36:00,668
- Overall.
- Her serves are strong.

846
00:36:00,893 --> 00:36:04,072
She's scored a lot as a one-point server.

847
00:36:04,396 --> 00:36:06,040
I used to be a huge fan of hers.

848
00:36:06,832 --> 00:36:09,444
And there's her, Seon Ok.

849
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:11,478
- Seon Ok is on the team too.
- She's on the team.

850
00:36:11,837 --> 00:36:13,748
She's young, but really tough.

851
00:36:14,005 --> 00:36:15,673
You can't let her energy overwhelm you.

852
00:36:16,435 --> 00:36:17,981
You probably know this about Red Sparks,

853
00:36:18,362 --> 00:36:20,168
but they collapse in the blink of an eye
when they do.

854
00:36:20,169 --> 00:36:22,219
That's frustrated me so many times.

855
00:36:22,601 --> 00:36:24,955
We need to take advantage
when that happens.

856
00:36:25,341 --> 00:36:27,958
If the game gets stuck in a rut,
Coach Ko Hee Jin...

857
00:36:28,447 --> 00:36:30,213
changes everything around...

858
00:36:30,413 --> 00:36:32,559
and causes confusion for the opponents.

859
00:36:33,119 --> 00:36:36,346
But I don't think that'll affect us much.

860
00:36:36,593 --> 00:36:37,825
We just need to keep our rhythm.

861
00:36:38,558 --> 00:36:39,870
He knows them so well.

862
00:36:40,755 --> 00:36:42,239
I've been watching them for 20 years now,

863
00:36:42,781 --> 00:36:45,424
- and I know our team.
- "Our team?"

864
00:36:46,031 --> 00:36:47,031
Excuse me?

865
00:36:47,277 --> 00:36:49,131
You still have Red Sparks
in your heart, don't you?

866
00:36:49,217 --> 00:36:50,704
It's in his blood.

867
00:36:50,705 --> 00:36:55,852
I always lose my voice after our games,
which never even happens at my concerts.

868
00:36:56,067 --> 00:36:58,722
I wish you'd see
how sincere my dedication is, just once.

869
00:36:58,965 --> 00:37:01,792
Win or lose, there's nothing in it for me.

870
00:37:02,093 --> 00:37:04,845
Why nothing in it for you?
If we lose, you lose too.

871
00:37:05,024 --> 00:37:06,418
It seems like you're rooting
for the Red Sparks.

872
00:37:07,457 --> 00:37:09,132
Nothing in it for you?
If we win, you win too.

873
00:37:09,192 --> 00:37:12,211
Right. There's a lot in it for me.
Our love and support.

874
00:37:12,224 --> 00:37:13,938
You're right. I'm sorry.
I take that back.

875
00:37:14,157 --> 00:37:17,641
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs! Thank you.

876
00:37:19,176 --> 00:37:21,845
(Going against another pro team)

877
00:37:22,413 --> 00:37:24,415
(To overcome the crisis,)

878
00:37:25,416 --> 00:37:29,420
(Wonder Dogs are going all out.)

879
00:37:30,054 --> 00:37:33,274
(And here's another one giving their all.)

880
00:37:33,275 --> 00:37:34,834
Hey!

881
00:37:36,027 --> 00:37:37,027
Hold on!

882
00:37:38,095 --> 00:37:39,697
(Eyes wide open)

883
00:37:40,297 --> 00:37:41,999
(Falling down)

884
00:37:42,132 --> 00:37:43,333
(Get the ball!)

885
00:37:43,734 --> 00:37:46,837
(Captain Pyo is going
through especially tough training today.)

886
00:37:47,312 --> 00:37:48,472
You're pushing yourself too hard.

887
00:37:48,692 --> 00:37:50,241
I know. I'm exhausted.

888
00:37:50,611 --> 00:37:51,611
We don't have much time.

889
00:37:52,091 --> 00:37:53,331
You won't have much time to train soon.

890
00:37:53,464 --> 00:37:54,912
You won't be able to train
like this forever.

891
00:37:56,647 --> 00:37:59,116
(The night before the game)

892
00:37:59,182 --> 00:38:04,755
If you think about it, this could be
the last match of your volleyball career.

893
00:38:05,042 --> 00:38:06,229
In your case,

894
00:38:07,191 --> 00:38:11,381
you had to retire unexpectedly, right?

895
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:15,265
I retired because I wanted to.
I'd been saying I would.

896
00:38:16,347 --> 00:38:19,169
But still,
it doesn't matter when I retired.

897
00:38:19,519 --> 00:38:22,606
I think I would've always had regrets.

898
00:38:25,172 --> 00:38:29,272
- I could've played for another two years.
- Of course.

899
00:38:29,398 --> 00:38:31,682
That thought does cross my mind
from time to time.

900
00:38:32,317 --> 00:38:34,770
Really? Then I think if we...

901
00:38:35,404 --> 00:38:37,821
really make Wonder Dogs an official team,

902
00:38:39,076 --> 00:38:41,658
you should start playing again.

903
00:38:41,976 --> 00:38:46,430
I might even get
a proper farewell game there.

904
00:38:47,064 --> 00:38:48,532
And to be honest,

905
00:38:48,779 --> 00:38:50,501
- I had to quit so suddenly.
- I know.

906
00:38:51,351 --> 00:38:55,973
Honestly, giving up
my 15-year volleyball career...

907
00:38:56,338 --> 00:38:59,143
wasn't easy at all.

908
00:39:00,010 --> 00:39:01,645
It was just so sad.

909
00:39:02,197 --> 00:39:03,714
Sad and upsetting.

910
00:39:04,423 --> 00:39:08,602
But in the end, it was my choice.

911
00:39:09,888 --> 00:39:12,181
Thanks to Wonder Dogs,

912
00:39:12,288 --> 00:39:14,194
if I get an opportunity to play again,

913
00:39:14,974 --> 00:39:18,121
I'll really try to...

914
00:39:18,461 --> 00:39:19,847
wrap things up nicely.

915
00:39:19,848 --> 00:39:23,300
(Ending on a good note)

916
00:39:24,186 --> 00:39:25,705
I want to beat the Red Sparks.

917
00:39:28,112 --> 00:39:29,112
Me too.

918
00:39:39,644 --> 00:39:41,746
(Daejeon Chungmu Gymnasium)

919
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:53,524
(The Wonder Dogs are
at the Red Sparks' home court.)

920
00:39:54,492 --> 00:39:57,462
(And here's Seung Ju.)

921
00:40:00,698 --> 00:40:03,668
(Her first time back here
since retiring four months ago)

922
00:40:07,519 --> 00:40:08,752
As I walked in,

923
00:40:09,039 --> 00:40:11,111
I walked slowly and looked around.

924
00:40:11,118 --> 00:40:12,777
I greeted my photo too.

925
00:40:13,225 --> 00:40:16,837
I thought, "Just a few months ago,"

926
00:40:16,838 --> 00:40:19,050
"I came here every day
to play volleyball."

927
00:40:19,358 --> 00:40:23,722
And I'm back here sooner
than I thought I'd be, playing again.

928
00:40:24,203 --> 00:40:26,203
So it was kind of...

929
00:40:26,437 --> 00:40:27,926
a mix of feelings.

930
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:33,731
(The locker room where she used
to get ready in her Red Sparks uniform)

931
00:40:35,345 --> 00:40:36,734
I had a lot of thoughts on my mind.

932
00:40:36,968 --> 00:40:40,767
Just a few months ago,
I was teammates with these players,

933
00:40:41,254 --> 00:40:43,474
but now I'm playing against them.

934
00:40:43,647 --> 00:40:45,693
It felt really strange.

935
00:40:49,547 --> 00:40:52,417
(The Red Sparks coaches' waiting room)

936
00:40:52,639 --> 00:40:54,552
- Hello.
- You're all here.

937
00:40:57,288 --> 00:41:01,359
(Stepping in with orange ties
around their necks)

938
00:41:01,391 --> 00:41:02,391
Ouch.

939
00:41:03,104 --> 00:41:04,596
What's with the orange ties?

940
00:41:04,617 --> 00:41:06,280
- What's with the orange tie?
- Well, you know.

941
00:41:06,386 --> 00:41:08,787
- We're on Team Wonder Dogs now.
- Oh, Wonder Dogs.

942
00:41:08,788 --> 00:41:11,001
Yes, Wonder Dogs.
Do you want to sit there?

943
00:41:11,020 --> 00:41:12,020
No.

944
00:41:12,886 --> 00:41:14,739
Yes, relive the memories.

945
00:41:17,135 --> 00:41:18,428
So, about today...

946
00:41:19,001 --> 00:41:20,214
Are you going all out today?

947
00:41:20,861 --> 00:41:22,861
I actually arranged the lineup...

948
00:41:23,279 --> 00:41:26,046
based on the Wonder Dogs' level.

949
00:41:26,440 --> 00:41:28,656
- What is our level?
- Yes, what is the Wonder Dogs' level?

950
00:41:28,993 --> 00:41:31,460
- What about us?
- So your best players are coming?

951
00:41:32,260 --> 00:41:35,396
We're sending out
our Futures team members today.

952
00:41:35,832 --> 00:41:39,234
If you're only sending Futures players,

953
00:41:39,432 --> 00:41:41,269
that means Park Eun Jin
and other pro players.

954
00:41:41,984 --> 00:41:46,207
They're here.
Eun Jin, Seon Woo, and Hye Min.

955
00:41:46,423 --> 00:41:47,742
Let's see how the first set goes.

956
00:41:48,110 --> 00:41:49,150
How it goes?

957
00:41:49,537 --> 00:41:51,113
If things get tough, then we might switch.

958
00:41:51,114 --> 00:41:53,236
(Things might change
if the game doesn't go their way.)

959
00:41:53,243 --> 00:41:55,239
In that case, we can adjust.

960
00:41:55,592 --> 00:41:57,385
Are they starting in the first set?

961
00:41:57,579 --> 00:41:59,754
The starting lineup is...

962
00:41:59,786 --> 00:42:01,432
made up of Futures players.

963
00:42:01,598 --> 00:42:02,757
Got it.

964
00:42:02,825 --> 00:42:05,727
Do you think it'll be close,
or totally your lead?

965
00:42:05,756 --> 00:42:07,032
We'll probably play
more comfortably today.

966
00:42:07,037 --> 00:42:08,396
I might even cross my legs
during the game.

967
00:42:10,265 --> 00:42:13,535
- We heard some information too.
- Where did you hear it?

968
00:42:14,269 --> 00:42:15,704
The key players weren't there.

969
00:42:16,855 --> 00:42:19,681
Yes, Suwon Special City's key players were
absent in our last game.

970
00:42:19,890 --> 00:42:21,743
So, what's your prediction
for today's game?

971
00:42:21,824 --> 00:42:23,078
- Three to zero.
- "Three to zero?"

972
00:42:23,576 --> 00:42:25,347
- The Red Sparks win.
- "The Red Sparks win."

973
00:42:26,696 --> 00:42:29,056
They were totally looking down on us.

974
00:42:29,163 --> 00:42:31,153
It really ticked me off.

975
00:42:31,154 --> 00:42:32,702
- They did from the beginning.
- That's good news.

976
00:42:33,888 --> 00:42:35,455
(Yes, let your guard down.)

977
00:42:35,502 --> 00:42:37,488
It was hard to hold it in, you know?

978
00:42:37,489 --> 00:42:38,687
They kept talking down to us.

979
00:42:38,688 --> 00:42:41,396
This is tricky.
They can't afford to lose either.

980
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:44,520
What'll they do if they lose?

981
00:42:44,607 --> 00:42:46,999
We'll give them something
to think about, I guess.

982
00:42:46,999 --> 00:42:49,304
We'll give them a headache.

983
00:42:50,271 --> 00:42:51,541
(The Wonder Dogs locker room)

984
00:42:51,555 --> 00:42:52,555
Come in.

985
00:42:53,455 --> 00:42:55,843
I brought some red ginseng
to give you a boost.

986
00:42:55,844 --> 00:42:59,807
(Red ginseng to boost your energy)

987
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:01,627
Nothing like red ginseng
to boost your energy.

988
00:43:02,350 --> 00:43:04,787
(Recharging with red ginseng)

989
00:43:04,794 --> 00:43:07,164
- Have you tried red ginseng, Enkhsoyol?
- No.

990
00:43:07,177 --> 00:43:08,984
- Have you tried red ginseng, Tamira?
- Thank you.

991
00:43:09,003 --> 00:43:11,993
- Do you know what red ginseng is?
- I know.

992
00:43:12,336 --> 00:43:15,063
- Ginseng.
- Yes, it's good for your body.

993
00:43:16,076 --> 00:43:18,366
- What do you think?
- It's really convenient.

994
00:43:19,668 --> 00:43:21,412
(Conveniently recharging before the game)

995
00:43:23,638 --> 00:43:26,940
(Three wins, two losses)

996
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:28,707
Two straight knockout wins!

997
00:43:28,960 --> 00:43:32,093
Keeping up the momentum, we'll challenge
the pro team for a three-game streak.

998
00:43:32,179 --> 00:43:35,016
It's the showdown between the Wonder Dogs
and the Red Sparks.

999
00:43:35,158 --> 00:43:39,432
With me are Suk Ja and Manager Seung Kwan,
a Red Sparks expert.

1000
00:43:39,451 --> 00:43:41,078
- Hello.
- Hello.

1001
00:43:41,098 --> 00:43:44,588
I'm Seung Kwan, the Wonder Dogs' manager.
Happy to be here.

1002
00:43:44,601 --> 00:43:47,429
The opponents are a very strong team.

1003
00:43:47,442 --> 00:43:50,874
Let's look at the differences
between these two teams.

1004
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:54,540
Well, if we're talking
about the Red Sparks,

1005
00:43:54,839 --> 00:43:58,040
to put it in terms of the idol world,

1006
00:43:58,346 --> 00:44:01,876
you could say they're a mega team
from a major agency.

1007
00:44:02,145 --> 00:44:04,145
A veteran idol group that's stayed
consistently active.

1008
00:44:04,772 --> 00:44:09,151
But the Wonder Dogs are
like a smaller group from a small agency.

1009
00:44:09,577 --> 00:44:13,154
That's their image,
so it's easy to underestimate them.

1010
00:44:13,502 --> 00:44:17,708
But in fact, Seventeen is one of those
so-called small-agency miracle teams.

1011
00:44:18,102 --> 00:44:22,369
I dare say the Wonder Dogs will show
us that miracle today too.

1012
00:44:22,582 --> 00:44:24,833
Now, let's briefly...

1013
00:44:24,834 --> 00:44:27,854
go through our strategy breakdown.

1014
00:44:27,855 --> 00:44:29,855
- Yes, okay.
- Yes.

1015
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:31,500
Among professional women's
volleyball teams,

1016
00:44:31,834 --> 00:44:34,042
they've got
the most national team players.

1017
00:44:34,173 --> 00:44:36,411
My beloved Red Sparks
have the most players.

1018
00:44:36,412 --> 00:44:39,714
- You should be careful.
- "My Red Sparks team?"

1019
00:44:39,763 --> 00:44:41,516
- Not "our."
- Did I say that again?

1020
00:44:41,589 --> 00:44:43,568
Darn it. Not "our," but "their."

1021
00:44:43,952 --> 00:44:45,688
"Their?"

1022
00:44:45,722 --> 00:44:48,523
Their Red Sparks team...

1023
00:44:48,598 --> 00:44:52,360
- has the most national team players.
- That's right.

1024
00:44:53,164 --> 00:44:56,764
Recently, Jeon Da Bin was
named to the U21 national team.

1025
00:44:56,803 --> 00:44:59,500
She's an amazing player.
And in this season's championship,

1026
00:44:59,603 --> 00:45:02,504
Shin Eun Ji scored 29 points
with her serves.

1027
00:45:02,856 --> 00:45:07,108
Seon Ok was also the second overall pick
in the first round of the 2023-24 season.

1028
00:45:07,409 --> 00:45:09,744
She joined the pro team
with high expectations.

1029
00:45:10,912 --> 00:45:13,982
(Choi Seo Hyun)

1030
00:45:16,887 --> 00:45:18,987
Let's go home relaxed today.

1031
00:45:19,026 --> 00:45:22,553
- Yes, let's do it.
- One, two, three. Let's go!

1032
00:45:26,494 --> 00:45:28,830
(The Wonder Dogs warming up)

1033
00:45:34,837 --> 00:45:36,571
Tae Young, is silent warm up your thing?

1034
00:45:36,937 --> 00:45:38,039
- Sorry?
- Is that your thing?

1035
00:45:38,663 --> 00:45:40,223
Come on, Seung Ju. Give us a shout!

1036
00:45:40,923 --> 00:45:41,923
Hello.

1037
00:45:42,316 --> 00:45:43,629
I mean, come on.

1038
00:45:51,759 --> 00:45:53,137
Their moves aren't bad.

1039
00:45:54,504 --> 00:45:55,890
Maybe I shouldn't have said three to zero.

1040
00:45:56,191 --> 00:45:58,393
(Laughing)

1041
00:45:59,763 --> 00:46:00,763
Look at them.

1042
00:46:02,980 --> 00:46:04,449
Tae Young, did you practice a lot?

1043
00:46:04,648 --> 00:46:06,545
Yes, we practice a lot.

1044
00:46:06,768 --> 00:46:07,967
- Every day?
- Yes.

1045
00:46:07,967 --> 00:46:09,611
We stay in the training camp together.

1046
00:46:10,303 --> 00:46:11,981
We do three hours of weight training,

1047
00:46:12,004 --> 00:46:14,349
and in the afternoons,
we work on ball skills.

1048
00:46:14,373 --> 00:46:16,418
Watching the players run today,

1049
00:46:16,841 --> 00:46:18,419
they look light on their feet.

1050
00:46:19,010 --> 00:46:20,020
Their form has improved a lot.

1051
00:46:20,912 --> 00:46:22,356
- It improved a lot?
- Yes.

1052
00:46:24,182 --> 00:46:25,025
Hi.

1053
00:46:25,316 --> 00:46:27,027
Hey, Coach Kim.

1054
00:46:27,051 --> 00:46:28,128
Out of the blue?

1055
00:46:28,152 --> 00:46:29,363
(Shaking hands)

1056
00:46:29,387 --> 00:46:30,722
I look forward to a good game.

1057
00:46:31,422 --> 00:46:32,499
You've come well prepared, right?

1058
00:46:32,724 --> 00:46:34,035
We did our best.

1059
00:46:34,058 --> 00:46:36,169
I heard that you're underestimating
our team.

1060
00:46:37,061 --> 00:46:38,739
Who leaked so much information?

1061
00:46:38,763 --> 00:46:39,850
You think we're an easy target?

1062
00:46:39,884 --> 00:46:41,095
That's not true.

1063
00:46:41,118 --> 00:46:42,363
You will regret underestimating us today.

1064
00:46:42,387 --> 00:46:44,798
- Oh, hi.
- Are you on their team too?

1065
00:46:44,822 --> 00:46:45,932
I'm supporting the Wonder Dogs now.

1066
00:46:45,957 --> 00:46:46,967
- He's our manager.
- Really?

1067
00:46:46,991 --> 00:46:48,459
You were a Red Sparks fan
through and through.

1068
00:46:48,626 --> 00:46:50,170
But I'm with them today.

1069
00:46:50,661 --> 00:46:52,706
- Are you sure?
- I won't hold back if I need to protest.

1070
00:46:53,431 --> 00:46:55,576
- I hope we have a good game.
- Let's play fair and square.

1071
00:47:00,672 --> 00:47:03,417
When I stepped into the court today,

1072
00:47:04,042 --> 00:47:06,320
it felt a bit different.

1073
00:47:07,118 --> 00:47:10,030
It felt somewhat different.

1074
00:47:10,621 --> 00:47:12,999
After all, it's my former team,

1075
00:47:13,290 --> 00:47:14,968
and I've always played on that court...

1076
00:47:15,593 --> 00:47:21,007
against other teams with those players.

1077
00:47:21,098 --> 00:47:23,276
But today, with the net between us,
facing them as the opponent,

1078
00:47:24,068 --> 00:47:26,613
it really hit me emotionally.

1079
00:47:28,672 --> 00:47:32,051
(The warmup session is over.)

1080
00:47:32,076 --> 00:47:34,421
Every set we lose,
the training will increase.

1081
00:47:35,246 --> 00:47:37,357
- Okay!
- You have to play with that mindset.

1082
00:47:37,481 --> 00:47:40,026
- Way to go.
- We're professionals, right?

1083
00:47:40,050 --> 00:47:41,561
- Yes!
- Let's go!

1084
00:47:41,585 --> 00:47:43,329
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1085
00:47:44,388 --> 00:47:45,565
Let's gather around.

1086
00:47:45,689 --> 00:47:46,799
Play with confidence.

1087
00:47:47,158 --> 00:47:49,169
- Victory is ours!
- Wonder Dogs!

1088
00:47:49,960 --> 00:47:52,639
The Wonder Dogs currently have
3 wins and 2 losses.

1089
00:47:52,663 --> 00:47:54,574
Only two games remain.

1090
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:59,846
If they secure a victory
against the Red Sparks today,

1091
00:48:00,404 --> 00:48:02,282
they'll have 4 wins and 2 losses,

1092
00:48:02,306 --> 00:48:04,417
ensuring the team's survival.

1093
00:48:04,441 --> 00:48:06,653
That's right. They won't be disbanded.

1094
00:48:06,677 --> 00:48:08,889
- We will survive as well, then.
- That's great.

1095
00:48:09,747 --> 00:48:12,292
A majority of wins.
That's all I can think about.

1096
00:48:12,583 --> 00:48:14,995
Since our goal is to become
the eighth team in the pro league,

1097
00:48:15,019 --> 00:48:17,831
we absolutely have to win this match.

1098
00:48:18,155 --> 00:48:19,632
Our players have improved enough,

1099
00:48:19,657 --> 00:48:25,439
and I believe we can compete
against pro teams,

1100
00:48:25,462 --> 00:48:27,006
so I'm really excited for today's match.

1101
00:48:30,134 --> 00:48:31,144
Let's have a good game.

1102
00:48:33,771 --> 00:48:35,949
Let me go over today's lineups
for both teams.

1103
00:48:35,973 --> 00:48:38,985
First, the lineup for the Wonder Dogs.

1104
00:48:39,101 --> 00:48:42,905
From position one, setter Koo Sol,
outside hitter Pyo Seung Ju,

1105
00:48:43,115 --> 00:48:44,658
middle blocker Moon Myoung Hwa,

1106
00:48:45,182 --> 00:48:47,026
opposite spiker Han Song Hee,

1107
00:48:47,451 --> 00:48:51,498
outside hitter Enkhsoyol,
and middle blocker Kim Hyeon Jeong.

1108
00:48:52,189 --> 00:48:54,925
(Starting lineup)

1109
00:48:55,859 --> 00:48:58,171
And the lineup for the Red Sparks.

1110
00:48:58,171 --> 00:48:59,776
Starting from position one,
outside hitter Jeon Da Bin,

1111
00:49:00,164 --> 00:49:01,508
middle blocker Lee Ho Bin,

1112
00:49:01,732 --> 00:49:03,443
opposite spiker Shin Eun Ji,

1113
00:49:03,801 --> 00:49:05,478
outside hitter Gwak Seon Ok,

1114
00:49:06,303 --> 00:49:07,680
middle blocker An Ye Rim,

1115
00:49:07,938 --> 00:49:09,516
and setter Choi Seo Hyun.

1116
00:49:10,374 --> 00:49:12,986
(Starting lineup)

1117
00:49:13,010 --> 00:49:14,287
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's go!

1118
00:49:14,311 --> 00:49:16,556
- Way to go!
- We can do this.

1119
00:49:16,580 --> 00:49:18,291
Let's go.

1120
00:49:18,315 --> 00:49:20,284
- Let's go!
- Yes!

1121
00:49:21,118 --> 00:49:22,095
We've got this.

1122
00:49:23,087 --> 00:49:25,132
For the Wonder Dogs' survival,

1123
00:49:25,389 --> 00:49:27,600
and for the first win against a pro team,

1124
00:49:27,958 --> 00:49:31,938
they'll be facing the Red Sparks today.

1125
00:49:31,962 --> 00:49:33,506
(Wonder Dogs vs. Red Sparks)

1126
00:49:33,530 --> 00:49:36,509
They struggled a lot
during the match against the Altos.

1127
00:49:36,634 --> 00:49:39,279
Back then, it was only the second game,

1128
00:49:39,303 --> 00:49:41,815
so the team wasn't fully in sync yet,

1129
00:49:41,839 --> 00:49:43,717
and their confidence was a bit low.

1130
00:49:43,741 --> 00:49:48,155
The Wonder Dogs back then and today are
clearly different.

1131
00:49:48,178 --> 00:49:49,522
They're completely different.

1132
00:49:49,546 --> 00:49:51,224
(Forget about the old Wonder Dogs.)

1133
00:49:51,382 --> 00:49:54,428
(First set, Red Sparks 0 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1134
00:49:56,020 --> 00:49:59,166
(Koo Sol,
released from the Red Sparks in 2020)

1135
00:49:59,556 --> 00:50:00,800
Sol must be nervous.

1136
00:50:02,293 --> 00:50:03,503
She used to play for the Red Sparks.

1137
00:50:04,428 --> 00:50:06,840
(She started her career
with the Red Sparks.)

1138
00:50:06,864 --> 00:50:08,875
Don't lose your focus in the beginning.

1139
00:50:09,700 --> 00:50:11,745
(Instructing a targeted serve
to Zone Three)

1140
00:50:12,303 --> 00:50:14,481
(Target zone)

1141
00:50:15,139 --> 00:50:17,451
Sol's serve kicks off the match.

1142
00:50:17,475 --> 00:50:18,385
The first set begins now!
My ball.

1143
00:50:20,334 --> 00:50:21,188
Seo Hyun.

1144
00:50:22,746 --> 00:50:23,623
Spike.

1145
00:50:23,847 --> 00:50:24,757
It's successful.

1146
00:50:24,782 --> 00:50:26,593
(Eun Ji's spike point)

1147
00:50:26,750 --> 00:50:28,928
Great!

1148
00:50:30,254 --> 00:50:31,164
Nice job.

1149
00:50:32,222 --> 00:50:36,002
Eun Ji, the left-handed opposite spiker,
is definitely powerful.

1150
00:50:36,026 --> 00:50:36,803
Indeed.

1151
00:50:37,828 --> 00:50:38,872
Three players.

1152
00:50:38,896 --> 00:50:39,773
(Strong)

1153
00:50:42,032 --> 00:50:44,077
Why did you serve to the libero?

1154
00:50:44,868 --> 00:50:46,379
- Or you should've aimed in between.
- Okay.

1155
00:50:46,403 --> 00:50:48,748
(Scolding her for deviating from the plan)

1156
00:50:48,772 --> 00:50:49,482
Okay.
Let's go!

1157
00:50:50,374 --> 00:50:54,120
Focus on a good reception,
and then we'll go for it right away.

1158
00:50:54,345 --> 00:50:55,722
A serve by Ho Bin.

1159
00:50:58,148 --> 00:50:58,958
Go!

1160
00:50:58,982 --> 00:51:00,126
- Get it!
- Song Hee.

1161
00:51:00,517 --> 00:51:01,661
Sol's back toss.

1162
00:51:01,985 --> 00:51:02,853
To Seung Ju!

1163
00:51:04,321 --> 00:51:05,231
She dug it.

1164
00:51:05,255 --> 00:51:06,499
Let's go for a point!

1165
00:51:08,659 --> 00:51:09,502
Push over!

1166
00:51:09,760 --> 00:51:11,604
But they defended it
and go for an attack again.

1167
00:51:11,795 --> 00:51:12,638
Seon Ok!

1168
00:51:12,663 --> 00:51:15,041
(A spike from Seon Ok)

1169
00:51:15,065 --> 00:51:16,009
It's successful.

1170
00:51:16,033 --> 00:51:17,944
(First set, Red Sparks 2 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1171
00:51:17,968 --> 00:51:19,212
Seon Ok is strong.

1172
00:51:19,670 --> 00:51:21,848
- Great!
- Nice job!

1173
00:51:21,872 --> 00:51:23,983
Myoung Hwa, do not spread!

1174
00:51:24,007 --> 00:51:26,219
Sol, don't show the toss early.
Wait for the right timing.

1175
00:51:26,243 --> 00:51:28,321
- If you show it too soon, they'll attack.
- Okay.

1176
00:51:28,979 --> 00:51:30,690
If they hit to predictable spots,

1177
00:51:30,714 --> 00:51:32,358
the opponent can defend every time...

1178
00:51:33,183 --> 00:51:35,261
because they're a pro team.

1179
00:51:36,587 --> 00:51:38,732
You need to put the ball up
for the setter.

1180
00:51:40,791 --> 00:51:42,268
Nice serve!

1181
00:51:42,826 --> 00:51:45,705
(The second serve by Ho Bin)

1182
00:51:46,497 --> 00:51:47,674
Hey, get it!

1183
00:51:48,165 --> 00:51:51,111
(The single toss was offbeat.)

1184
00:51:51,568 --> 00:51:52,578
Set it!

1185
00:51:53,637 --> 00:51:54,514
Set it!
Eun Ji.

1186
00:51:56,640 --> 00:51:57,984
It's successful.

1187
00:51:58,509 --> 00:51:59,920
They score consecutively.

1188
00:52:00,377 --> 00:52:01,187
Nice.

1189
00:52:01,211 --> 00:52:04,323
(First set, Red Sparks 3 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1190
00:52:04,715 --> 00:52:06,393
(In the blink of an eye,
the gap grew to three points.)

1191
00:52:06,416 --> 00:52:10,696
- Eun Ji is incredibly powerful.
- Right.

1192
00:52:11,422 --> 00:52:15,203
Both Eun Ji and Seon Ok are...

1193
00:52:15,226 --> 00:52:19,038
currently playing
for the youth national team,

1194
00:52:19,062 --> 00:52:20,740
and their attacking skills are impressive.

1195
00:52:20,764 --> 00:52:22,775
The opposite spiker position is...

1196
00:52:22,799 --> 00:52:24,810
usually filled by foreign players,

1197
00:52:24,835 --> 00:52:26,913
- so they simply haven't had many chances.
- Exactly.

1198
00:52:27,204 --> 00:52:30,383
From the start, the Wonder Dogs have been
giving up the momentum.

1199
00:52:30,974 --> 00:52:33,052
Let's run it through once.

1200
00:52:33,076 --> 00:52:34,487
Let's go!

1201
00:52:36,200 --> 00:52:38,211
(The server is Ho Bin again.)

1202
00:52:38,502 --> 00:52:40,013
The serve is short!

1203
00:52:40,036 --> 00:52:41,280
Move your feet!

1204
00:52:41,738 --> 00:52:43,983
- Serve.
- It's Ho Bin's serve again.

1205
00:52:44,608 --> 00:52:45,385
Go.

1206
00:52:46,343 --> 00:52:47,187
Sol.

1207
00:52:47,544 --> 00:52:48,745
Seung Ju.
In 1, 2.

1208
00:52:48,769 --> 00:52:50,389
(It's defended.)

1209
00:52:50,515 --> 00:52:52,091
- They kept the ball alive.
- Eun Ji!

1210
00:52:52,983 --> 00:52:53,960
(Eun Ji's powerful spike)

1211
00:52:53,984 --> 00:52:56,162
She hits it over. It's a touch-out.

1212
00:52:57,888 --> 00:53:02,735
(First set, Red Sparks 4 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1213
00:53:04,995 --> 00:53:06,973
Just one, please!

1214
00:53:08,732 --> 00:53:11,678
Seung Ju is having
a bit of a tough time today.

1215
00:53:13,203 --> 00:53:15,581
(Ho Bin's fourth serve)

1216
00:53:15,605 --> 00:53:16,348
Mine.
Sol.

1217
00:53:17,741 --> 00:53:18,818
Seung Ju received it.

1218
00:53:18,842 --> 00:53:20,787
(It's received nicely...)

1219
00:53:20,810 --> 00:53:23,088
(and set skillfully.)

1220
00:53:23,647 --> 00:53:24,691
Song Hee!

1221
00:53:24,714 --> 00:53:25,491
Hit it!

1222
00:53:26,917 --> 00:53:27,727
It's out.

1223
00:53:28,118 --> 00:53:28,961
It's a touch-out!

1224
00:53:29,252 --> 00:53:29,995
No?

1225
00:53:30,787 --> 00:53:32,565
It's out.

1226
00:53:33,123 --> 00:53:36,202
The Wonder Dogs start
by giving up five points.

1227
00:53:39,197 --> 00:53:41,698
They're having a bit of a rough start
to the game again today.

1228
00:53:42,232 --> 00:53:44,076
Just one point, please!

1229
00:53:45,869 --> 00:53:48,114
(Ho Bin's fifth serve)

1230
00:53:50,373 --> 00:53:51,917
- Go get it!
- Hye In.

1231
00:53:52,042 --> 00:53:53,019
Get it!

1232
00:53:53,043 --> 00:53:56,456
(Which way will the toss go?)

1233
00:53:56,713 --> 00:53:57,590
Seung Ju.

1234
00:53:59,182 --> 00:54:00,693
It's blocked.

1235
00:54:01,707 --> 00:54:07,199
(First set, Red Sparks 6 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1236
00:54:07,224 --> 00:54:08,624
That's it, Seon Ok.

1237
00:54:08,624 --> 00:54:10,257
(You're the best.)

1238
00:54:10,457 --> 00:54:13,324
- Gwak Seon Ok!
- Gwak Seon Ok!

1239
00:54:16,091 --> 00:54:20,124
I guess the team knows me too well.

1240
00:54:21,191 --> 00:54:23,424
My former teammates know me well.

1241
00:54:23,424 --> 00:54:25,857
We trained together every day.

1242
00:54:26,057 --> 00:54:29,357
They know where and how I'll hit
when I attack...

1243
00:54:29,557 --> 00:54:31,824
as they learned it inside out.

1244
00:54:32,191 --> 00:54:36,357
That's why at first, I had no idea...

1245
00:54:36,382 --> 00:54:39,649
how to attack them,
even though I tried to solve it.

1246
00:54:39,991 --> 00:54:44,191
Because I couldn't work that out
at the start of the game,

1247
00:54:44,491 --> 00:54:47,024
I was emotionally struggling.

1248
00:54:47,756 --> 00:54:49,023
It wasn't easy.

1249
00:54:49,657 --> 00:54:50,657
Nice!

1250
00:54:50,657 --> 00:54:55,291
(And this is the opponent's home court.)

1251
00:54:56,324 --> 00:54:58,724
We had no substitute player.

1252
00:54:58,724 --> 00:55:01,157
(What's worse, they lack
a substitute player.)

1253
00:55:01,157 --> 00:55:02,991
Everyone was losing confidence,

1254
00:55:03,157 --> 00:55:06,991
and even the setter,
the key player, also struggled.

1255
00:55:07,257 --> 00:55:12,457
I thought the hitters wouldn't be able
to attack at this rate.

1256
00:55:12,457 --> 00:55:13,657
(Coach Kim makes a decision.)

1257
00:55:14,157 --> 00:55:16,757
Jin. Lee Jin!

1258
00:55:17,624 --> 00:55:19,524
They change the setter in the end.

1259
00:55:19,524 --> 00:55:23,124
(Koo Sol out, Lee Jin in)

1260
00:55:26,724 --> 00:55:29,257
Ye Rim, she's good at quick attacks.

1261
00:55:29,257 --> 00:55:31,891
- Watch for quicks before anything else.
- Yes, Coach.

1262
00:55:33,257 --> 00:55:34,291
Watch the long ones!

1263
00:55:35,791 --> 00:55:38,491
(Lee Ho Bin's sixth serve)

1264
00:55:39,524 --> 00:55:41,257
- Go!
- Lee Jin.

1265
00:55:41,257 --> 00:55:42,591
(She tries a quick attack.)

1266
00:55:42,591 --> 00:55:44,891
She launches a B-quick,
but the ball is saved.

1267
00:55:46,757 --> 00:55:50,057
Gwak Seon Ok spikes, and it's a touch out.

1268
00:55:51,257 --> 00:55:55,391
(First set, Red Sparks 7 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1269
00:55:56,424 --> 00:55:59,257
(Even the substitute player is...)

1270
00:55:59,791 --> 00:56:03,024
(analyzed thoroughly
by the pro runner-up team)

1271
00:56:03,157 --> 00:56:05,957
We keep it inside the court.

1272
00:56:06,157 --> 00:56:07,791
Stay in your positions!

1273
00:56:10,291 --> 00:56:11,757
(The formidable barrier
of the professional level)

1274
00:56:11,757 --> 00:56:13,257
It's zero to seven.

1275
00:56:15,091 --> 00:56:17,924
(Lee Ho Bin's seventh serve)

1276
00:56:18,924 --> 00:56:20,457
Koo Hye In receives it smoothly.

1277
00:56:20,591 --> 00:56:21,591
Lee Jin.

1278
00:56:21,591 --> 00:56:22,857
(The other team has a single block.)

1279
00:56:22,857 --> 00:56:23,882
Han Song Hee!

1280
00:56:23,907 --> 00:56:24,822
(Open up!)

1281
00:56:25,224 --> 00:56:26,557
(It's dug up.)

1282
00:56:26,791 --> 00:56:27,824
The defence was successful.

1283
00:56:28,457 --> 00:56:30,957
Gwak Seon Ok uses a tip,
but she slides in to receive it.

1284
00:56:31,291 --> 00:56:33,591
They save the ball, and it rebounds.

1285
00:56:33,591 --> 00:56:34,857
Slow down!

1286
00:56:36,491 --> 00:56:37,491
Han Song Hee!

1287
00:56:38,024 --> 00:56:39,724
It's blocked!

1288
00:56:39,841 --> 00:56:42,257
(Shin Eun Ji, the ace, scores
with a block.)

1289
00:56:43,491 --> 00:56:44,824
Oh, my gosh.

1290
00:56:45,357 --> 00:56:47,337
Oh, my gosh. No!

1291
00:56:48,891 --> 00:56:51,624
(They did everything
to prepare for the match...)

1292
00:56:52,024 --> 00:56:54,657
(as they're competing with the pro team.)

1293
00:56:54,857 --> 00:56:57,491
It's the first technical time out
of the first set,

1294
00:56:57,491 --> 00:56:59,724
but the Wonder Dogs couldn't get
a single point.

1295
00:57:00,591 --> 00:57:02,957
Today is their sixth match.

1296
00:57:03,724 --> 00:57:05,924
But they always struggle
at the start of the game.

1297
00:57:05,924 --> 00:57:07,091
You're right.

1298
00:57:07,391 --> 00:57:11,257
This may be the Wonder Dogs'
greatest weakness.

1299
00:57:11,257 --> 00:57:13,257
- They lose many points at the start.
- That's right.

1300
00:57:14,157 --> 00:57:15,891
They need to turn the tide now.

1301
00:57:15,891 --> 00:57:16,991
(Now, it's eight to zero.)

1302
00:57:16,991 --> 00:57:18,424
This is making me crazy.

1303
00:57:20,950 --> 00:57:23,784
(A reality too shocking to believe)

1304
00:57:24,724 --> 00:57:26,710
Don't you think when you play?

1305
00:57:27,691 --> 00:57:29,546
Look at the scores. What are they?

1306
00:57:30,291 --> 00:57:31,724
What are the points?

1307
00:57:32,824 --> 00:57:34,491
- I said, "What are the points?"
- It's eight to zero.

1308
00:57:34,724 --> 00:57:35,986
Eight to zero, right?

1309
00:57:36,124 --> 00:57:39,024
- You have to work on easy ones first.
- Yes, Coach.

1310
00:57:39,024 --> 00:57:40,157
Concentrate.

1311
00:57:40,424 --> 00:57:42,157
- Let's do it again.
- Again!

1312
00:57:42,157 --> 00:57:44,124
One point at a time!

1313
00:57:44,491 --> 00:57:46,391
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's do it again!

1314
00:57:46,391 --> 00:57:48,432
It was a single block.
What's with the hesitation?

1315
00:57:48,724 --> 00:57:49,724
Yes!

1316
00:57:49,724 --> 00:57:52,424
What's scaring you?

1317
00:57:52,857 --> 00:57:53,957
Yes, Coach!

1318
00:57:55,457 --> 00:57:58,508
If the shot misses,
get ready to cover and rebound.

1319
00:57:58,533 --> 00:57:59,913
Let's start from there.

1320
00:58:01,291 --> 00:58:04,391
(The Wonder Dogs are hanging
on the cliff.)

1321
00:58:04,824 --> 00:58:09,991
(The Red Sparks are formidable,
like an unbreakable wall.)

1322
00:58:10,257 --> 00:58:11,975
(They must close the eight-point lead...)

1323
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:14,032
(and get the momentum back.)

1324
00:58:14,057 --> 00:58:15,291
Okay!

1325
00:58:17,224 --> 00:58:19,391
Lee Ho Bin continues to serve.

1326
00:58:19,391 --> 00:58:21,291
(Lee Ho Bin's eighth serve)

1327
00:58:22,957 --> 00:58:24,291
The reception was a bit unstable.

1328
00:58:25,584 --> 00:58:28,873
An open spike,
and the block was effective.

1329
00:58:30,791 --> 00:58:32,824
Gwak Seon Ok hits, and Koo Hye In digs.

1330
00:58:33,432 --> 00:58:35,599
Setup by Lee Jin,
followed by Song Hee's dink!

1331
00:58:35,624 --> 00:58:37,324
- Set it up!
- They defended it.

1332
00:58:37,624 --> 00:58:38,857
Hit it!

1333
00:58:40,764 --> 00:58:42,397
It was a tip, but they dug it up!

1334
00:58:42,791 --> 00:58:45,157
They must play calmly.
Han Song Hee spikes!

1335
00:58:45,157 --> 00:58:46,791
(An intense, merciless rally)

1336
00:58:46,791 --> 00:58:47,791
The ball is up.

1337
00:58:47,791 --> 00:58:49,157
(Just break through!)

1338
00:58:49,491 --> 00:58:50,824
Enkhsoyol digs at the back.

1339
00:58:50,924 --> 00:58:54,857
(The chance goes to Seung Ju!)

1340
00:58:54,857 --> 00:58:55,857
Pyo Seung Ju.

1341
00:58:57,578 --> 00:58:58,367
(It's dug up.)

1342
00:58:58,391 --> 00:58:59,857
The rally goes on.

1343
00:59:00,110 --> 00:59:01,405
Hit it!

1344
00:59:01,657 --> 00:59:02,657
Spike!

1345
00:59:02,657 --> 00:59:05,424
(We must save the ball in the air.)

1346
00:59:06,791 --> 00:59:08,424
(A chance earned through sheer tenacity)

1347
00:59:09,557 --> 00:59:10,857
Han Song Hee's high ball!

1348
00:59:11,991 --> 00:59:14,524
(Are they saving this?)

1349
00:59:15,057 --> 00:59:16,591
(They save it.)

1350
00:59:16,891 --> 00:59:19,524
It's a free ball.
It's a great opportunity.

1351
00:59:19,524 --> 00:59:20,591
Koo Hye In.

1352
00:59:20,991 --> 00:59:22,191
Let's go!

1353
00:59:22,757 --> 00:59:24,757
Lee Jin back tosses to Seung Ju.

1354
00:59:24,757 --> 00:59:25,791
(Go, Seung Ju!)

1355
00:59:25,791 --> 00:59:26,791
Spike!

1356
00:59:28,091 --> 00:59:29,091
(Blocked again)

1357
00:59:29,091 --> 00:59:31,257
Choi Seo Hyun manages to defend again.

1358
00:59:32,191 --> 00:59:36,324
(The ace gets the chance.)

1359
00:59:37,257 --> 00:59:38,857
It's a touch out.

1360
00:59:39,691 --> 00:59:42,091
(First set, Red Sparks 9 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1361
00:59:42,091 --> 00:59:43,657
Way to go, Shin Eun Ji!

1362
00:59:43,657 --> 00:59:45,357
Nice one, Eun Ji!

1363
00:59:46,091 --> 00:59:49,691
After a long rally,
the Wonder Dogs lose another point.

1364
00:59:49,691 --> 00:59:51,657
(A nine-point gap after a fierce rally)

1365
00:59:51,657 --> 00:59:54,057
(We must catch up at all costs.)

1366
00:59:56,991 --> 00:59:58,691
Jin, what did I tell you to do?

1367
00:59:58,691 --> 00:59:59,724
Attack.

1368
01:00:01,591 --> 01:00:05,624
(Jin and Enkhsoyol exchange
signs for a back attack.)

1369
01:00:09,091 --> 01:00:10,457
It's zero to nine.

1370
01:00:10,457 --> 01:00:11,557
(Lee Ho Bin's ninth serve)

1371
01:00:11,557 --> 01:00:12,557
Mine!

1372
01:00:13,224 --> 01:00:14,457
Back attack!

1373
01:00:16,357 --> 01:00:17,957
- Enkhsoyol!
- Tip!

1374
01:00:18,924 --> 01:00:19,957
A tip shot from the middle back.

1375
01:00:22,266 --> 01:00:23,932
(They get their first point
with a tip from the middle back.)

1376
01:00:23,957 --> 01:00:25,522
We need more scores.

1377
01:00:28,610 --> 01:00:31,677
That's not a score we should have allowed!

1378
01:00:32,824 --> 01:00:36,524
It wasn't a flawless play,

1379
01:00:36,624 --> 01:00:39,057
but they attacked
with a different pattern.

1380
01:00:39,224 --> 01:00:42,391
So the Red Sparks were out
of their positions.

1381
01:00:43,524 --> 01:00:46,124
They came a long way
to get their first point.

1382
01:00:47,024 --> 01:00:48,812
I told you about the back attack,
didn't I?

1383
01:00:49,257 --> 01:00:51,014
- Why wouldn't you do it?
- Understood.

1384
01:00:51,824 --> 01:00:53,591
They should catch up step by step.

1385
01:00:53,591 --> 01:00:55,357
- Serve.
- Pyo Seung Ju serves.

1386
01:00:56,576 --> 01:00:57,488
Mine!

1387
01:01:00,557 --> 01:01:01,557
Nice pass.

1388
01:01:01,791 --> 01:01:03,224
(Choi Seo Hyun's perfect back toss)

1389
01:01:03,624 --> 01:01:05,691
Shin Eun Ji scores with a block out.

1390
01:01:07,157 --> 01:01:08,824
- Nice toss!
- Nice!

1391
01:01:09,457 --> 01:01:11,157
- Nice pass, Seo Hyun.
- Yes, Coach.

1392
01:01:11,157 --> 01:01:13,091
Hit it deep like that.

1393
01:01:13,091 --> 01:01:14,757
It was a great pass from Choi Seo Hyun.

1394
01:01:14,757 --> 01:01:18,157
(They're nine points apart again,
thanks to Setter Choi Seo Hyun.)

1395
01:01:19,224 --> 01:01:21,424
(Walking)

1396
01:01:21,857 --> 01:01:22,857
Nice, Eun Ji.

1397
01:01:25,624 --> 01:01:28,257
(The server is a U-21 national athlete.)

1398
01:01:28,324 --> 01:01:30,124
Last V-League season,

1399
01:01:30,357 --> 01:01:33,724
she scored 19 aces
in the 36 games she played.

1400
01:01:33,891 --> 01:01:35,024
That's Shin Eun Ji.

1401
01:01:36,791 --> 01:01:38,491
(Spinning the ball)

1402
01:01:39,691 --> 01:01:40,691
(Sighing)

1403
01:01:44,024 --> 01:01:45,435
Who's in front of you, Enkhsoyol?

1404
01:01:46,757 --> 01:01:48,405
Yes. I've got the short ones.

1405
01:01:49,924 --> 01:01:52,157
- Stay on the left first.
- Okay.

1406
01:01:52,157 --> 01:01:53,824
(They adjust their positions as if on cue)

1407
01:01:54,291 --> 01:01:57,957
Shin Eun Ji is left-handed,
and she hits like this.

1408
01:01:59,024 --> 01:02:01,024
You have to turn left.

1409
01:02:01,024 --> 01:02:02,324
- Understood?
- Yes.

1410
01:02:02,324 --> 01:02:04,124
Turn more. That's it.

1411
01:02:04,124 --> 01:02:06,024
You need to stay turned.

1412
01:02:06,024 --> 01:02:07,157
- Got it?
- Yes.

1413
01:02:08,124 --> 01:02:09,259
We should turn.

1414
01:02:10,191 --> 01:02:12,824
- Let's turn.
- Receive the ball first.

1415
01:02:12,824 --> 01:02:14,157
(They are positioned and facing left,
as planned)

1416
01:02:16,291 --> 01:02:17,324
Serve!

1417
01:02:21,224 --> 01:02:22,757
- Mine.
- Go, Seung Ju!

1418
01:02:22,757 --> 01:02:24,157
- Seung Ju receives it smoothly.
- Great!

1419
01:02:25,591 --> 01:02:27,457
(Lee Jin sets the ball.)

1420
01:02:27,724 --> 01:02:29,000
Jin, a toss like that?

1421
01:02:29,024 --> 01:02:29,646
Perfect!

1422
01:02:31,724 --> 01:02:33,457
Enkhsoyol's tip.

1423
01:02:33,457 --> 01:02:34,584
Enkhsoyol is amazing.

1424
01:02:34,609 --> 01:02:36,124
(Her tip disrupts the receiving formation)

1425
01:02:37,857 --> 01:02:39,091
(Shin Eun Ji spikes from the back.)

1426
01:02:39,091 --> 01:02:41,324
She hits from the back, but it's out.

1427
01:02:41,891 --> 01:02:43,191
My mistake.

1428
01:02:43,524 --> 01:02:44,524
Come on.

1429
01:02:44,857 --> 01:02:46,091
Okay!

1430
01:02:46,491 --> 01:02:49,024
One play at a time. It's fine.

1431
01:02:50,691 --> 01:02:54,203
They are persistently using tips
to challenge the Red Sparks' defense.

1432
01:02:55,691 --> 01:02:58,191
You can't defend like that.

1433
01:02:58,191 --> 01:03:00,291
- Yes, Coach!
- Understood? Focus.

1434
01:03:00,757 --> 01:03:03,924
(One point earned,
closing the gap to eight)

1435
01:03:04,091 --> 01:03:06,391
One by one. Take your time!

1436
01:03:06,724 --> 01:03:08,518
Moon Myoung Hwa serves.

1437
01:03:13,124 --> 01:03:14,191
One, two!

1438
01:03:14,857 --> 01:03:15,957
A quick attack to the middle.

1439
01:03:16,557 --> 01:03:17,557
They saved it.

1440
01:03:19,324 --> 01:03:21,557
Another tip coming.
Will the defense break down again?

1441
01:03:22,491 --> 01:03:23,957
Choi Hyo Seo sets it up.

1442
01:03:25,491 --> 01:03:26,857
(We'll prepare for the block)

1443
01:03:26,857 --> 01:03:28,457
Hold your hands firm!

1444
01:03:34,057 --> 01:03:36,857
- That's it. Point!
- All right!

1445
01:03:38,324 --> 01:03:42,257
(They successfully stop Gwak Seon Ok,
a U-21 player)

1446
01:03:42,924 --> 01:03:44,888
Here comes the Wonder Dogs' strength.

1447
01:03:44,913 --> 01:03:45,667
Keep it going!

1448
01:03:45,691 --> 01:03:48,324
(Their strength has now reduced the gap
to seven points.)

1449
01:03:48,324 --> 01:03:50,224
This team plays a simple game.

1450
01:03:50,492 --> 01:03:53,497
Why are you hesitating here?
Where should you focus your block?

1451
01:03:54,059 --> 01:03:55,892
Go to the hitter quickly.

1452
01:03:56,259 --> 01:03:58,492
Don't linger there,
Myoung Hwa and Hyeon Jeong.

1453
01:03:58,492 --> 01:03:59,926
(Form a double block on the side)

1454
01:03:59,926 --> 01:04:01,626
(The middle attack is rare.
Don't fall for it.)

1455
01:04:01,650 --> 01:04:03,073
Where should you focus your block?

1456
01:04:03,818 --> 01:04:06,921
(Double block on the side)

1457
01:04:07,355 --> 01:04:08,366
Nice!

1458
01:04:08,390 --> 01:04:10,091
(The performance analysts are pleased.)

1459
01:04:10,929 --> 01:04:11,948
Let's do it again!

1460
01:04:11,948 --> 01:04:13,628
(Kim Hyeon Jeong, middle blocker)

1461
01:04:14,284 --> 01:04:16,290
When she jumps,
you can dink it over there.

1462
01:04:17,465 --> 01:04:19,834
(His counter-strategy
against the Wonder Dogs is the dink)

1463
01:04:21,035 --> 01:04:23,337
(Second serve by Myoung Hwa)

1464
01:04:23,649 --> 01:04:24,761
Myoung Hwa again.

1465
01:04:27,508 --> 01:04:29,677
(She moves to the side
without hesitation.)

1466
01:04:32,387 --> 01:04:34,060
- Spike.
- That's it.

1467
01:04:34,193 --> 01:04:35,292
Here they go again.

1468
01:04:37,579 --> 01:04:39,586
(Tip for block!)

1469
01:04:42,462 --> 01:04:43,738
Another block on the tip!

1470
01:04:44,971 --> 01:04:46,798
That's it, they're coming again.

1471
01:04:47,904 --> 01:04:49,330
- Hit it!
- The third attempt.

1472
01:04:49,331 --> 01:04:50,865
(She moves exactly
as the coach instructed.)

1473
01:04:52,967 --> 01:04:54,156
(Dang it!)

1474
01:04:54,157 --> 01:04:56,030
Hyeon Jeong's block works
three times in a row!

1475
01:04:56,337 --> 01:04:57,438
No.

1476
01:04:58,859 --> 01:05:01,576
They switch direction,
to the left-handed Eun Ji!

1477
01:05:03,649 --> 01:05:06,280
- Back attack.
- It's out.

1478
01:05:06,281 --> 01:05:08,649
(Scored by line out)

1479
01:05:09,283 --> 01:05:10,745
Nice!

1480
01:05:10,746 --> 01:05:12,019
Okay!

1481
01:05:12,078 --> 01:05:15,322
Guys, if you're not up for the block,
watch out for the tip.

1482
01:05:15,837 --> 01:05:19,429
Wonder Dogs are narrowing the gap,
one point at a time, gaining momentum.

1483
01:05:19,603 --> 01:05:22,103
Our team's strong suit is blocking.

1484
01:05:22,176 --> 01:05:26,400
Wonder Dogs are creating chances
by forcing errors.

1485
01:05:28,121 --> 01:05:29,537
No! Seriously!

1486
01:05:29,718 --> 01:05:30,546
My mistake.

1487
01:05:30,571 --> 01:05:34,208
(The game isn't going
as it did in the beginning.)

1488
01:05:34,790 --> 01:05:36,978
Seon Ok, where were you even looking
when you spiked?

1489
01:05:37,348 --> 01:05:39,013
- You need to watch it.
- Okay!

1490
01:05:40,556 --> 01:05:42,506
It's 4 to 10, a six-point gap.

1491
01:05:44,685 --> 01:05:45,685
Myoung Hwa!

1492
01:05:47,288 --> 01:05:48,871
(Third serve by Myoung Hwa)

1493
01:05:48,884 --> 01:05:51,392
They need to keep building chances off
of Myoung Hwa's serve.

1494
01:05:55,534 --> 01:05:56,534
(Grunting)

1495
01:05:56,770 --> 01:05:58,143
It's out.

1496
01:06:01,843 --> 01:06:03,477
It's in!

1497
01:06:03,549 --> 01:06:06,374
- It's in!
- Score!

1498
01:06:06,403 --> 01:06:08,576
A point directly from Myoung Hwa's serve.

1499
01:06:09,076 --> 01:06:10,778
(Whenever she serves,)

1500
01:06:11,445 --> 01:06:14,315
(the opponents dive to the floor.)

1501
01:06:14,582 --> 01:06:16,918
(Here goes Myoung Hwa again.)

1502
01:06:17,618 --> 01:06:20,187
(Clenching their fists)

1503
01:06:26,661 --> 01:06:30,331
(Unbelievable!)

1504
01:06:31,032 --> 01:06:33,439
- Myoung Hwa!
- Well done.

1505
01:06:33,465 --> 01:06:35,670
That drop was crazy.

1506
01:06:39,307 --> 01:06:42,944
(Now it's a five-point gap,
thanks to her precise serves.)

1507
01:06:43,377 --> 01:06:44,912
(And...)

1508
01:06:46,914 --> 01:06:48,983
(Captain Seung Ju shows
her biggest smile for the first time.)

1509
01:06:49,210 --> 01:06:51,645
Let's catch up one by one.

1510
01:06:51,703 --> 01:06:52,409
That's right.

1511
01:06:53,176 --> 01:06:57,523
Myoung Hwa's serves are difficult
to receive.

1512
01:06:58,275 --> 01:07:02,008
She's starting to make
her presence felt in this match.

1513
01:07:03,409 --> 01:07:04,596
The score is now 5 to 10.

1514
01:07:05,599 --> 01:07:07,668
(But as the game resumes,)

1515
01:07:08,402 --> 01:07:11,405
(the opponents pull ahead again,
widening the gap back to six.)

1516
01:07:11,972 --> 01:07:15,342
(We need to widen the gap even further.)

1517
01:07:16,724 --> 01:07:19,914
Ye Rim, they tend to jump with her
and then go for a double block.

1518
01:07:20,316 --> 01:07:21,805
The short one's in front of you.

1519
01:07:23,084 --> 01:07:25,086
Just spike it her way.

1520
01:07:26,320 --> 01:07:28,756
(You mean, me?)

1521
01:07:28,889 --> 01:07:32,460
Coach Ko targets the shorter player,
Song Hee, for attack.

1522
01:07:32,461 --> 01:07:35,330
(Target Song Hee when attacking.)

1523
01:07:39,633 --> 01:07:40,767
Go!

1524
01:07:41,678 --> 01:07:42,678
Song Hee!

1525
01:07:43,253 --> 01:07:45,576
- She'll go for the tip!
- It's a dink!

1526
01:07:52,413 --> 01:07:54,448
- Spike!
- That's good.

1527
01:07:57,451 --> 01:08:01,155
(She was targeted because of her height.)

1528
01:08:04,691 --> 01:08:07,428
- Let's do it again!
- Pass it to her again!

1529
01:08:08,404 --> 01:08:09,582
Jump!

1530
01:08:10,831 --> 01:08:12,299
(Leap)

1531
01:08:13,852 --> 01:08:15,202
Spike!

1532
01:08:16,843 --> 01:08:18,239
She digs the powerful spike!

1533
01:08:20,107 --> 01:08:22,609
(They've already decided on their target.)

1534
01:08:23,911 --> 01:08:25,192
But it's blocked.

1535
01:08:25,980 --> 01:08:27,315
(Groaning)

1536
01:08:27,704 --> 01:08:28,337
Again!

1537
01:08:28,909 --> 01:08:29,909
Pass it to her again!

1538
01:08:30,327 --> 01:08:32,120
- Hit it!
- Here goes her attack again.

1539
01:08:32,420 --> 01:08:33,521
Go for it!

1540
01:08:34,466 --> 01:08:37,892
- This time, it's a tip! Success!
- Score!

1541
01:08:39,376 --> 01:08:42,330
Wasn't it obvious she'd tip
after two spikes?

1542
01:08:42,396 --> 01:08:44,164
Okay! We got this.

1543
01:08:44,475 --> 01:08:45,766
That's it.

1544
01:08:48,191 --> 01:08:51,438
Song Hee, well done, nice spikes.

1545
01:08:51,598 --> 01:08:54,942
Keep it up, just swing
as much as you want. It's okay.

1546
01:08:55,182 --> 01:08:57,377
(Nice spikes!)

1547
01:08:57,991 --> 01:08:59,713
During my volleyball career,

1548
01:08:59,896 --> 01:09:02,383
there's one thing
that's always haunted me.

1549
01:09:02,803 --> 01:09:05,762
It's always my height.
Everything comes back to that.

1550
01:09:06,722 --> 01:09:10,548
I think she's too short
to make a pro team.

1551
01:09:10,694 --> 01:09:12,426
Song Hee is pretty short.

1552
01:09:12,887 --> 01:09:14,528
The short one's in front of you.

1553
01:09:16,035 --> 01:09:19,667
Because I'm short...

1554
01:09:19,998 --> 01:09:22,603
But you can't overcome height.

1555
01:09:23,070 --> 01:09:25,425
Is it even possible?

1556
01:09:26,127 --> 01:09:28,127
Here comes Song Hee with her spike.

1557
01:09:29,543 --> 01:09:33,080
(Coach Kim kept her eyes on Song Hee
when she was on a corporate team.)

1558
01:09:33,293 --> 01:09:35,399
She's not bad, though.

1559
01:09:36,044 --> 01:09:40,287
It's just too bad
that Song Hee isn't taller.

1560
01:09:40,754 --> 01:09:41,957
(How will she utilize
the shortest outside hitter?)

1561
01:09:41,964 --> 01:09:42,964
It's a shame.

1562
01:09:45,164 --> 01:09:49,696
Her serve, offense, and defense are
all good. That's impressive.

1563
01:09:51,710 --> 01:09:52,710
She's a reception-type right attacker.

1564
01:09:52,711 --> 01:09:54,869
Now, we'll go to the right.

1565
01:09:56,562 --> 01:10:00,867
(She practiced
both reception-type defense...)

1566
01:10:00,900 --> 01:10:04,268
(and right-side offense at the same time.)

1567
01:10:05,003 --> 01:10:08,223
I've been busy making excuses,
blaming my height.

1568
01:10:09,283 --> 01:10:12,386
(Now she's become an opposite hitter
who can also defend.)

1569
01:10:13,153 --> 01:10:14,661
(Song Hee, 172cm tall)

1570
01:10:14,695 --> 01:10:16,190
My height...

1571
01:10:17,081 --> 01:10:19,393
I don't care about that anymore.

1572
01:10:19,394 --> 01:10:21,062
(When did I ever care?)

1573
01:10:22,062 --> 01:10:25,232
(Small Giant, Han Song Hee)

1574
01:10:26,647 --> 01:10:28,335
Serve by Song Hee, the Small Giant.

1575
01:10:36,028 --> 01:10:39,913
- A point by serve! Han Song Hee!
- That was good!

1576
01:10:40,714 --> 01:10:41,714
Yes!

1577
01:10:42,814 --> 01:10:45,019
She's on a roll, her serves too!

1578
01:10:49,690 --> 01:10:51,225
(Shaking his head)

1579
01:10:52,359 --> 01:10:55,128
(Another serve by Song Hee)

1580
01:10:57,798 --> 01:10:59,566
It didn't touch her hand!

1581
01:11:00,267 --> 01:11:05,305
(The referee calls it a service point.)

1582
01:11:05,778 --> 01:11:08,472
Once Song Hee warms up,

1583
01:11:08,473 --> 01:11:12,513
the offense starts to click,
and her serves get even stronger.

1584
01:11:13,013 --> 01:11:16,090
(Thanks to Seung Ju,
the teammates are fully awake now.)

1585
01:11:16,129 --> 01:11:19,186
The score is down
to just a two-point difference.

1586
01:11:21,222 --> 01:11:24,681
That's going to make
the opponents nervous.

1587
01:11:25,960 --> 01:11:27,808
(Two more points to tie the game)

1588
01:11:27,809 --> 01:11:30,531
If we can just pull off
what we're capable of,

1589
01:11:30,740 --> 01:11:32,307
we'll win today's game.

1590
01:11:32,427 --> 01:11:34,168
That's what I realized.

1591
01:11:35,520 --> 01:11:37,632
As Coach Kim planned, blocking,
serving, and Song Hee's attacks...

1592
01:11:37,656 --> 01:11:40,041
start to work together
like gears in a machine.

1593
01:11:40,449 --> 01:11:42,142
Now all they need to do is
close that two-point gap.

1594
01:11:42,143 --> 01:11:45,946
(The last cog to close the gap.)

1595
01:11:47,055 --> 01:11:50,017
We need more attacks through the middle.

1596
01:11:50,618 --> 01:11:55,323
(Middle back-row attack)

1597
01:11:55,547 --> 01:11:58,226
Almost every Korean team has
the same strategies.

1598
01:11:58,680 --> 01:12:00,761
Their blocking and defense are
all similar.

1599
01:12:00,942 --> 01:12:02,139
What can you do now?

1600
01:12:02,163 --> 01:12:05,999
If you truly understand this,
you'll kill it out there.

1601
01:12:06,305 --> 01:12:08,832
Who has the advantage
when we go through the middle?

1602
01:12:09,345 --> 01:12:11,532
The ones on the left, right? So today,

1603
01:12:11,725 --> 01:12:15,175
we need to use the middle even more.

1604
01:12:15,364 --> 01:12:18,045
It won't work overseas
because they can read the play.

1605
01:12:18,564 --> 01:12:20,236
It's always a double block
wherever you attack.

1606
01:12:21,070 --> 01:12:23,384
Did you get it?
A setter needs to be smart.

1607
01:12:23,570 --> 01:12:25,762
But in Korea, that's not the case.
A setter doesn't need to be smart. Why?

1608
01:12:25,942 --> 01:12:29,923
Because it's always the same,
all you have to do is memorize!

1609
01:12:30,142 --> 01:12:33,160
They're all the same, the Asian teams.

1610
01:12:34,147 --> 01:12:37,517
(So far, Wonder Dogs haven't shown
a proper back attack.)

1611
01:12:37,542 --> 01:12:40,277
(Against Suwon Special City)

1612
01:12:40,302 --> 01:12:43,297
(And today's match)

1613
01:12:44,168 --> 01:12:49,142
Jin, set it up nicely
so they can spike it hard.

1614
01:12:49,985 --> 01:12:52,468
Seo Hyun, the worst is
when the ball gets too close to the net.

1615
01:12:52,851 --> 01:12:55,210
- Be precise.
- Okay.

1616
01:12:56,430 --> 01:12:59,849
The score was nine to zero earlier,
but now the gap's only two points.

1617
01:13:01,815 --> 01:13:04,151
(Careful serve)

1618
01:13:06,248 --> 01:13:08,141
Da Bin's spike.

1619
01:13:08,142 --> 01:13:09,322
Get it up!

1620
01:13:09,648 --> 01:13:12,119
Hye In's reception,
and here goes Enkhsoyol!

1621
01:13:12,426 --> 01:13:13,534
(Enkhsoyol's spike)

1622
01:13:13,535 --> 01:13:15,830
Spike! But it's defended.

1623
01:13:16,700 --> 01:13:18,628
Da Bin's tip.

1624
01:13:19,010 --> 01:13:20,390
- It's a feint.
- Feint!

1625
01:13:20,493 --> 01:13:22,908
- It's mine!
- Go for it!

1626
01:13:22,932 --> 01:13:24,838
Small Giant Song Hee is flying!

1627
01:13:26,573 --> 01:13:27,841
Darn it!

1628
01:13:28,318 --> 01:13:29,318
What are you doing?

1629
01:13:29,467 --> 01:13:30,873
Go for it!

1630
01:13:31,221 --> 01:13:32,221
A short one!

1631
01:13:32,246 --> 01:13:33,447
Enkhsoyol's back step.

1632
01:13:34,014 --> 01:13:35,382
(Here comes Enkhsoyol again!)

1633
01:13:36,850 --> 01:13:38,652
(Back attack)

1634
01:13:41,722 --> 01:13:43,347
(Exhaling)

1635
01:13:45,392 --> 01:13:47,361
(It's not Enkhsoyol.)

1636
01:13:47,458 --> 01:13:48,458
That's it. Nice set.

1637
01:13:53,758 --> 01:13:55,558
Seung Ju hits from the middle!

1638
01:13:55,558 --> 01:13:57,033
Trailing by just one point!

1639
01:13:57,324 --> 01:13:58,457
This is unbelievable.

1640
01:14:01,558 --> 01:14:03,158
Great! One more point!

1641
01:14:05,691 --> 01:14:10,658
(The momentum has completely shifted
to the Wonder Dogs' side.)

1642
01:14:10,658 --> 01:14:11,658
Nice job!

1643
01:14:11,658 --> 01:14:13,125
Jin, nice set!

1644
01:14:13,125 --> 01:14:14,225
That was a great set.

1645
01:14:14,225 --> 01:14:15,891
You can set it a bit higher.

1646
01:14:15,891 --> 01:14:17,520
Give them a bit more room to swing, okay?

1647
01:14:18,325 --> 01:14:19,489
What are you doing, Da Bin?

1648
01:14:21,458 --> 01:14:24,658
(Tension rising on Red Sparks' side)

1649
01:14:24,658 --> 01:14:26,725
Just hit like you always do.

1650
01:14:26,725 --> 01:14:28,364
- Yes, coach.
- Don't try anything fancy.

1651
01:14:29,391 --> 01:14:31,225
It's not perfect yet,

1652
01:14:31,225 --> 01:14:34,958
but our current back-row offense
is scoring points.

1653
01:14:34,958 --> 01:14:36,625
(Blocking, small giant,
serves, middle-back attacks)

1654
01:14:37,125 --> 01:14:39,391
- Enkhsoyol, your hits are getting low.
- Setter, go...

1655
01:14:39,858 --> 01:14:42,391
Hit it high, okay? From the top.

1656
01:14:42,825 --> 01:14:44,225
Or Enkhsoyol!

1657
01:14:44,225 --> 01:14:45,491
You can aim for the gap too.

1658
01:14:45,491 --> 01:14:48,458
When you attack. When you're on offense.

1659
01:14:48,458 --> 01:14:49,491
In between, okay.

1660
01:14:51,591 --> 01:14:53,925
(Get caught,)

1661
01:14:53,925 --> 01:14:55,125
They've narrowed the gap.

1662
01:14:55,125 --> 01:14:56,058
No change!

1663
01:14:56,058 --> 01:14:57,558
(Or catch.)

1664
01:14:57,825 --> 01:14:59,191
Get ready to pass the ball.

1665
01:14:59,191 --> 01:15:01,525
(Only one point to tie it up)

1666
01:15:03,358 --> 01:15:04,391
Da Bin's receive.

1667
01:15:04,958 --> 01:15:05,925
Hit it, Eun Ji.

1668
01:15:05,925 --> 01:15:07,158
(Eun Ji's back-row attack)

1669
01:15:07,591 --> 01:15:08,491
A back-row spike.

1670
01:15:08,491 --> 01:15:10,258
Nice dig! Great defense!

1671
01:15:10,258 --> 01:15:11,791
Cover her! Get in!

1672
01:15:11,791 --> 01:15:13,325
Mine! Left!

1673
01:15:14,458 --> 01:15:15,358
Come in!

1674
01:15:15,358 --> 01:15:17,091
- Can we tie the score?
- Enkhsoyol!

1675
01:15:17,091 --> 01:15:17,925
Enkhsoyol!

1676
01:15:19,825 --> 01:15:21,125
(Giving away an easy ball)

1677
01:15:21,125 --> 01:15:21,991
Darn it!

1678
01:15:21,991 --> 01:15:23,125
No, Enkhsoyol!

1679
01:15:23,458 --> 01:15:24,691
A free ball!

1680
01:15:28,325 --> 01:15:29,325
Spike!
Nice dig!

1681
01:15:30,191 --> 01:15:31,491
Okay, good! Nice one, Hyeon Jeong!

1682
01:15:31,491 --> 01:15:33,291
It's coming again, Hyeon Jeong!

1683
01:15:35,025 --> 01:15:37,125
- Spike!
- One more, please!

1684
01:15:38,391 --> 01:15:39,425
She digs it!

1685
01:15:41,958 --> 01:15:42,891
Mine!

1686
01:15:42,916 --> 01:15:44,050
Hit it deep!

1687
01:15:44,075 --> 01:15:45,033
Hit it!

1688
01:15:45,758 --> 01:15:47,791
Song Hee, go for the rebound!

1689
01:15:47,791 --> 01:15:50,191
(It's Wonder Dogs' ball again.)

1690
01:15:53,058 --> 01:15:55,958
Enkhsoyol, aim for the gap
when you attack.

1691
01:15:55,958 --> 01:15:57,591
(Jump and scan for a gap!)

1692
01:15:59,625 --> 01:16:01,625
(But the gap is closed.)

1693
01:16:03,658 --> 01:16:05,558
(Found it!)

1694
01:16:07,391 --> 01:16:08,725
Enkhsoyol!

1695
01:16:08,725 --> 01:16:10,725
- Great attack!
- It's tied now!

1696
01:16:10,725 --> 01:16:12,658
We made up nine points!

1697
01:16:14,358 --> 01:16:16,758
(Finally tied)

1698
01:16:16,758 --> 01:16:18,391
Good job, guys.

1699
01:16:19,691 --> 01:16:21,625
(So exhilarating)

1700
01:16:21,625 --> 01:16:24,091
It's tied! It's freaking tied!

1701
01:16:24,725 --> 01:16:26,391
(Good job, Enkhsoyol.)

1702
01:16:27,191 --> 01:16:31,291
Just keep doing what you're doing.
Aim for the gaps, sides, or middle.

1703
01:16:31,291 --> 01:16:32,825
- Nice job.
- Thanks.

1704
01:16:34,325 --> 01:16:36,091
- Song Hwa, nice defense.
- Yes, Coach.

1705
01:16:37,691 --> 01:16:39,725
Jin, you're doing great too. Stay calm.

1706
01:16:39,725 --> 01:16:43,858
The Wonder Dogs' blocking
and defense are syncing up now,

1707
01:16:43,858 --> 01:16:45,258
and the game's heating up.

1708
01:16:45,258 --> 01:16:49,425
(We're back to square one.)

1709
01:16:50,325 --> 01:16:52,825
(The pro team gave up nine points.)

1710
01:16:53,658 --> 01:16:54,658
Unbelievable.

1711
01:16:56,625 --> 01:16:59,525
(On the verge of taking the lead)

1712
01:17:01,058 --> 01:17:01,925
Serve!

1713
01:17:01,950 --> 01:17:03,050
(Enkhsoyol's serve)

1714
01:17:04,425 --> 01:17:05,558
(A fast serve right on target)

1715
01:17:05,991 --> 01:17:07,925
(A quick counterattack)

1716
01:17:08,658 --> 01:17:09,791
(A whistle?)

1717
01:17:10,858 --> 01:17:13,125
(When Hyeon Jeong went up to block,)

1718
01:17:14,025 --> 01:17:16,491
(the net shook.)

1719
01:17:17,058 --> 01:17:19,258
(She touched the net on her way down.)

1720
01:17:19,925 --> 01:17:21,658
A net touch is called.

1721
01:17:23,558 --> 01:17:25,158
The players are in high spirits right now,

1722
01:17:25,158 --> 01:17:26,858
- but they can't get too carried away.
- You're right.

1723
01:17:27,958 --> 01:17:30,625
(Spotting a gap)

1724
01:17:31,825 --> 01:17:34,091
Da Bin, swing with confidence.

1725
01:17:34,091 --> 01:17:35,191
Just go for it.

1726
01:17:35,391 --> 01:17:37,091
(Okay.)

1727
01:17:37,091 --> 01:17:40,225
Myoung Hwa, watch their spacing.

1728
01:17:40,925 --> 01:17:43,858
(Red Sparks trying to widen the gap again)

1729
01:17:44,725 --> 01:17:45,691
It's falling.

1730
01:17:46,586 --> 01:17:47,401
(Hyeon Jeong digging)

1731
01:17:47,425 --> 01:17:48,458
Hyeon Jeong sets it.

1732
01:17:48,925 --> 01:17:50,591
(Seung Ju spikes.)

1733
01:17:50,591 --> 01:17:51,768
Seung Ju!

1734
01:17:53,025 --> 01:17:53,958
They dig it!

1735
01:17:54,691 --> 01:17:55,591
Are they countering now?

1736
01:17:55,591 --> 01:17:56,658
(Da Bin's powerful spike)

1737
01:18:00,258 --> 01:18:01,125
A net battle!

1738
01:18:02,691 --> 01:18:04,625
- Here!
- Run!

1739
01:18:04,991 --> 01:18:06,325
(Again, to Da Bin)

1740
01:18:06,325 --> 01:18:07,458
Da Bin spikes!

1741
01:18:08,825 --> 01:18:10,325
(A touch out?)

1742
01:18:10,325 --> 01:18:11,758
(No, we need to save it.)

1743
01:18:11,758 --> 01:18:12,925
Come on, get it!

1744
01:18:14,458 --> 01:18:17,591
(Straight out of bounds)

1745
01:18:17,591 --> 01:18:18,558
A touch out!

1746
01:18:18,558 --> 01:18:20,625
- Nice!
- Nice!

1747
01:18:20,625 --> 01:18:22,425
(Red Sparks lead by one point again.)

1748
01:18:23,358 --> 01:18:25,258
(Now's the perfect chance.)

1749
01:18:26,091 --> 01:18:27,225
Hye Min, come here!

1750
01:18:28,258 --> 01:18:29,225
Come on.

1751
01:18:29,225 --> 01:18:30,691
(A substitution?)

1752
01:18:31,325 --> 01:18:32,825
Serve, then move
to defense zone three.

1753
01:18:32,825 --> 01:18:33,658
Yes, Coach.

1754
01:18:34,225 --> 01:18:38,591
Coach Ko sends in Hye Min
earlier than expected.

1755
01:18:41,712 --> 01:18:42,958
They're here.

1756
01:18:42,958 --> 01:18:45,958
Eun Jin, Seon Woo, and Hye Min.

1757
01:18:46,557 --> 01:18:49,323
They're here,
but let's see how the game goes first.

1758
01:18:50,204 --> 01:18:53,671
- Red Sparks send in their ace player.
- Don't feel pressured.

1759
01:18:53,671 --> 01:18:55,738
(Sending in a national player
to keep their lead)

1760
01:18:56,004 --> 01:18:57,438
(Glancing)

1761
01:18:58,038 --> 01:19:00,538
Her serves are short and shaky.
Hye Min's up.

1762
01:19:00,538 --> 01:19:03,071
Hye Min's serves come slow.
You know that, right?

1763
01:19:03,071 --> 01:19:04,671
(Got it. Hye Min's serves are short.)

1764
01:19:05,071 --> 01:19:09,204
(Feeling the pressure)

1765
01:19:09,904 --> 01:19:11,971
(Hye Min serves.)

1766
01:19:17,671 --> 01:19:20,171
(The ball hits the net.)

1767
01:19:20,471 --> 01:19:22,304
(Will it end in a service error?)

1768
01:19:24,538 --> 01:19:27,771
An ace serve skims the net
and goes over for a point.

1769
01:19:28,771 --> 01:19:30,338
Red Sparks pull ahead!

1770
01:19:30,338 --> 01:19:32,204
(Keeping their lead
with consecutive points)

1771
01:19:32,504 --> 01:19:33,404
Myoung Hwa!

1772
01:19:35,271 --> 01:19:37,838
Myoung Hwa, how many times is this now?

1773
01:19:37,838 --> 01:19:40,204
Coach Yeon Koung must be
furious right now.

1774
01:19:40,204 --> 01:19:42,338
They struggled and finally closed the gap.

1775
01:19:43,938 --> 01:19:45,104
Da Bin with a strong spike!

1776
01:19:45,104 --> 01:19:47,938
(Helpless against the pro team's
powerful offense)

1777
01:19:47,938 --> 01:19:49,471
Skims the net and crosses over...

1778
01:19:49,471 --> 01:19:51,171
for an ace serve point.

1779
01:19:52,538 --> 01:19:56,238
(Taking back the lead is tough.)

1780
01:19:56,538 --> 01:19:59,804
(First set, Red Sparks 16
: Wonder Dogs 15)

1781
01:19:59,804 --> 01:20:01,438
- One by one, okay?
- Okay.

1782
01:20:01,438 --> 01:20:02,838
All we need is one point.

1783
01:20:02,838 --> 01:20:04,838
(Pro runner-up team is no pushover.)

1784
01:20:06,104 --> 01:20:09,238
(They need to find a way
out of this tough situation.)

1785
01:20:10,338 --> 01:20:14,171
(What move has the rookie coach prepared
for this moment?)

1786
01:20:22,304 --> 01:20:24,571
(Targeting serve to zone three)

1787
01:20:25,338 --> 01:20:27,671
(Zone 3)

1788
01:20:27,938 --> 01:20:30,571
(Inputting the signal)

1789
01:20:31,204 --> 01:20:32,104
Serve.

1790
01:20:32,104 --> 01:20:33,371
(Seung Ju's target serve)

1791
01:20:36,038 --> 01:20:37,038
Their receive is shaky.

1792
01:20:37,338 --> 01:20:38,271
Hit it!

1793
01:20:38,904 --> 01:20:39,738
Hit it hard!

1794
01:20:40,404 --> 01:20:41,204
Seon Ok!

1795
01:20:43,538 --> 01:20:45,304
(Did it break through?)

1796
01:20:49,004 --> 01:20:50,471
Hye In dives for the dig!

1797
01:20:50,471 --> 01:20:51,571
That's it!

1798
01:20:53,538 --> 01:20:55,704
(Going for the tip!)

1799
01:20:55,971 --> 01:20:56,771
Go! Hit it!
Eun Ji.

1800
01:20:58,871 --> 01:21:01,004
(Off the blockers' hands!)

1801
01:21:01,904 --> 01:21:02,871
She digs it!

1802
01:21:02,871 --> 01:21:04,538
(Hye In to the rescue again!)

1803
01:21:05,538 --> 01:21:06,804
Let's stay calm.

1804
01:21:06,804 --> 01:21:07,771
(Red Sparks' free ball)

1805
01:21:09,238 --> 01:21:10,738
(Seon Ok's powerful spike)

1806
01:21:11,838 --> 01:21:13,838
It's a short one, and Hye In sets it up!

1807
01:21:14,238 --> 01:21:15,938
(A chance created by Hye In)

1808
01:21:16,538 --> 01:21:17,471
Go!

1809
01:21:18,104 --> 01:21:20,171
(Just break through!)

1810
01:21:22,238 --> 01:21:24,104
Touch out!

1811
01:21:24,104 --> 01:21:25,538
It's tied again!

1812
01:21:25,971 --> 01:21:27,804
(Yes! We're tied!)

1813
01:21:28,038 --> 01:21:30,138
- Nice job, guys.
- Nice defense, Hye In.

1814
01:21:30,138 --> 01:21:31,938
Nice job, Hye In. Good work!

1815
01:21:33,571 --> 01:21:36,871
(Why is Coach Yeon Koung looking
so satisfied?)

1816
01:21:37,043 --> 01:21:40,952
Seon Ok hits diagonally more often
than Da Bin or Hye Min.

1817
01:21:40,977 --> 01:21:44,209
(She analyzed
the opponents' offense in detail.)

1818
01:21:44,256 --> 01:21:46,123
Listen closely.

1819
01:21:46,148 --> 01:21:49,988
So this forms an opposite square, right?

1820
01:21:50,485 --> 01:21:53,218
Watch for her diagonal hits.

1821
01:21:54,052 --> 01:21:55,852
(And while everyone was
focused on the front,)

1822
01:21:56,585 --> 01:21:58,718
(she stayed back and covered the court.)

1823
01:21:59,785 --> 01:22:02,585
Hye In's really impressing us today.

1824
01:22:05,252 --> 01:22:07,752
The Wonder Dogs finally score!

1825
01:22:07,752 --> 01:22:12,352
Hye In is standing out
with her remarkably steady play.

1826
01:22:12,952 --> 01:22:14,318
(Since the last Suwon Special City match,)

1827
01:22:15,752 --> 01:22:19,285
(Hye In has shown noticeable improvement.)

1828
01:22:20,452 --> 01:22:23,852
(A perfect offensive flow)

1829
01:22:24,918 --> 01:22:28,485
(And today, she's following
the coach's defensive strategy perfectly.)

1830
01:22:29,285 --> 01:22:31,685
Hye In is totally in the zone today!

1831
01:22:33,185 --> 01:22:34,518
Where the heck are you aiming?

1832
01:22:34,518 --> 01:22:36,018
Why are you aiming at players?

1833
01:22:36,718 --> 01:22:37,752
Come on.

1834
01:22:37,752 --> 01:22:39,218
(She blocked a pro player's attacks.)

1835
01:22:41,652 --> 01:22:46,285
(First set, Red Sparks 16
: Wonder Dogs 16)

1836
01:22:48,118 --> 01:22:49,018
Seon Ok.

1837
01:22:49,652 --> 01:22:52,252
That's such a sloppy hit.

1838
01:22:52,252 --> 01:22:53,152
Hit it harder.

1839
01:22:55,018 --> 01:22:58,685
(Red Sparks on offense)

1840
01:22:59,285 --> 01:23:04,418
(Wonder Dogs on defense)

1841
01:23:05,318 --> 01:23:08,818
(Only one more point to take the lead)

1842
01:23:09,552 --> 01:23:11,985
(Seung Ju serves.)

1843
01:23:12,618 --> 01:23:14,918
(A shaky receive)

1844
01:23:15,518 --> 01:23:17,285
(They set it and tip it over
from the middle.)

1845
01:23:17,885 --> 01:23:20,018
(Running over to dig)

1846
01:23:20,452 --> 01:23:22,585
(And passing it to setter Jin)

1847
01:23:22,885 --> 01:23:24,852
It's set high, and Enkhsoyol spikes!

1848
01:23:28,285 --> 01:23:30,652
(Seon Ok's spike)

1849
01:23:30,652 --> 01:23:31,685
Nice dig!

1850
01:23:31,685 --> 01:23:33,018
(Passing to the right)

1851
01:23:33,985 --> 01:23:36,352
(Runs right to cover!)

1852
01:23:36,352 --> 01:23:38,085
- Runs for the ball, and spikes!
- Song Hee!

1853
01:23:38,085 --> 01:23:39,785
(After the attack,)

1854
01:23:40,085 --> 01:23:41,752
(Hye In moves back into position.)

1855
01:23:41,752 --> 01:23:43,585
Red Sparks attack
through the middle again.

1856
01:23:43,985 --> 01:23:44,818
Eun Ji spikes.

1857
01:23:45,598 --> 01:23:46,654
Will they be able to save it?

1858
01:23:47,052 --> 01:23:49,469
(Is it left this time?)

1859
01:23:52,675 --> 01:23:55,042
(She was a step late.)

1860
01:23:55,042 --> 01:23:56,242
Great job!

1861
01:23:57,042 --> 01:23:58,042
Nice.

1862
01:23:59,542 --> 01:24:00,842
- I'm sorry.
- Nice play.

1863
01:24:04,109 --> 01:24:05,442
It's okay.

1864
01:24:07,975 --> 01:24:08,842
Nice.

1865
01:24:10,836 --> 01:24:13,269
(Who's the one that covers
the Wonder Dogs' back?)

1866
01:24:13,909 --> 01:24:19,575
(During the match against the Altos,
the team that released her)

1867
01:24:20,309 --> 01:24:22,909
(Defense failure)

1868
01:24:22,909 --> 01:24:25,009
(Failure)

1869
01:24:25,542 --> 01:24:28,609
(Another failure)

1870
01:24:30,075 --> 01:24:30,875
I'm sorry.

1871
01:24:31,475 --> 01:24:33,742
Hye In, sorry won't fix this.

1872
01:24:33,742 --> 01:24:35,375
Keep saying sorry,
and you'll lose the game.

1873
01:24:35,709 --> 01:24:37,509
- Set it high!
- Okay!

1874
01:24:38,809 --> 01:24:40,475
(In the end, she suffered
a humiliating defeat...)

1875
01:24:41,667 --> 01:24:43,934
(against her former teammates.)

1876
01:24:44,742 --> 01:24:46,975
- Are you hurt?
- No.

1877
01:24:46,975 --> 01:24:47,909
Then, why weren't you in the game?
Because I'm bad.

1878
01:24:50,542 --> 01:24:52,809
I must play better.

1879
01:24:52,809 --> 01:24:55,042
I will work even harder.

1880
01:24:55,042 --> 01:24:57,209
I will work harder.

1881
01:24:59,909 --> 01:25:02,509
(If 10 times aren't enough, I'll try 100.)

1882
01:25:02,684 --> 01:25:06,309
(If 100 aren't enough, I'll go for 1,000.)

1883
01:25:06,542 --> 01:25:08,409
(Even after all the teammates left
the court,)

1884
01:25:08,809 --> 01:25:11,142
(she stayed behind to practice alone.)

1885
01:25:13,075 --> 01:25:17,075
(Even when the production crew
completely packed up,)

1886
01:25:18,075 --> 01:25:21,109
(her questions kept coming.)

1887
01:25:21,134 --> 01:25:23,034
(Bye.)

1888
01:25:23,375 --> 01:25:24,542
Let me hit the slate!

1889
01:25:24,542 --> 01:25:25,475
In 1, 2, 3.

1890
01:25:25,742 --> 01:25:28,309
(And the day has come.)

1891
01:25:28,842 --> 01:25:30,309
(Hye In has successfully defended...)

1892
01:25:30,575 --> 01:25:31,909
(a total of 13 times)

1893
01:25:32,301 --> 01:25:33,934
(The highest across both teams)

1894
01:25:34,142 --> 01:25:35,775
(She could miss once in a while,)

1895
01:25:35,775 --> 01:25:38,353
(but it's all right.)

1896
01:25:39,442 --> 01:25:45,675
(We all trust you.)

1897
01:25:52,375 --> 01:25:53,481
The receive was a bit too short.

1898
01:25:55,942 --> 01:25:57,009
Da Bin, to the opposite side.

1899
01:25:57,009 --> 01:25:59,342
(The ball went past her teammate,)

1900
01:26:00,075 --> 01:26:03,409
(and the only one behind her is me.)

1901
01:26:08,975 --> 01:26:09,775
That's it.

1902
01:26:11,375 --> 01:26:13,375
(Jin gets the ball Hye In saved.)

1903
01:26:15,409 --> 01:26:17,642
Enkhsoyol's spike works!

1904
01:26:19,409 --> 01:26:21,042
The Wonder Dogs strike back!

1905
01:26:21,909 --> 01:26:24,742
Hye In must take credit for this!

1906
01:26:25,475 --> 01:26:28,542
In the pro league,
we rarely saw her on defense.

1907
01:26:29,475 --> 01:26:31,542
It was definitely the right call
to put her on defense.

1908
01:26:33,242 --> 01:26:35,342
(The coach is grinning too.)

1909
01:26:35,975 --> 01:26:38,709
(Hye In's defense lays the foundation.)

1910
01:26:39,642 --> 01:26:40,875
(Jin's toss)

1911
01:26:41,675 --> 01:26:43,809
Enkhsoyol's attack is successful!

1912
01:26:44,942 --> 01:26:47,175
(With the score of 20 to 20,
it's a tie again.)

1913
01:26:48,059 --> 01:26:51,326
(With solid defense,
the offense is going smoothly.)

1914
01:26:51,842 --> 01:26:53,709
- Enkhsoyol, target in between.
- Okay.

1915
01:26:55,609 --> 01:26:56,609
Serve.

1916
01:26:56,609 --> 01:26:57,742
(The biggest turning point
of the first set)

1917
01:26:59,475 --> 01:27:00,509
The serve is made.

1918
01:27:00,509 --> 01:27:01,975
(Let's go for the comeback hit!)

1919
01:27:02,175 --> 01:27:02,975
Hey.

1920
01:27:04,609 --> 01:27:05,509
A spike to the middle!
It's blocked!

1921
01:27:08,442 --> 01:27:09,975
(Jin's straight hit)

1922
01:27:09,975 --> 01:27:11,075
It's defended in the back row.

1923
01:27:12,409 --> 01:27:13,475
It's a chance ball.

1924
01:27:13,909 --> 01:27:14,709
Let's go.

1925
01:27:14,709 --> 01:27:16,609
Go for it.

1926
01:27:16,609 --> 01:27:17,542
Hye In's dig.

1927
01:27:17,542 --> 01:27:18,909
(Hye In's nice dig)

1928
01:27:19,175 --> 01:27:20,842
Jin tosses it backward.

1929
01:27:21,275 --> 01:27:22,409
Hyeon Jeong!

1930
01:27:24,375 --> 01:27:26,142
(Unstable defense)

1931
01:27:27,242 --> 01:27:29,275
(The ball is hit by Da Bin again.)

1932
01:27:31,509 --> 01:27:33,875
- A powerful spike once again!
- But it's out!

1933
01:27:34,528 --> 01:27:37,461
The referee calls it out.

1934
01:27:38,000 --> 01:27:40,033
(Great! It's out!)

1935
01:27:40,842 --> 01:27:43,175
(Finally, we turned the tables around!)

1936
01:27:43,175 --> 01:27:46,242
Now, the Wonder Dogs take the lead!

1937
01:27:47,975 --> 01:27:50,275
(Led by Hye In's ironclad defense,)

1938
01:27:51,509 --> 01:27:56,142
(the Wonder Dogs are exploiting
various attacking routes.)

1939
01:27:56,609 --> 01:27:58,142
They came back from 0 to 9.

1940
01:27:58,475 --> 01:27:59,775
It's astonishing.

1941
01:27:59,775 --> 01:28:01,675
(A huge comeback from 0 to 9)

1942
01:28:06,793 --> 01:28:09,326
Da Bin, seriously...

1943
01:28:09,326 --> 01:28:12,359
You've been hitting at the same timing
over and over.

1944
01:28:12,359 --> 01:28:13,293
Got it.

1945
01:28:13,659 --> 01:28:15,826
Use your strength and hit it higher.

1946
01:28:17,093 --> 01:28:17,959
Okay.

1947
01:28:19,426 --> 01:28:20,628
Enkhsoyol serves.

1948
01:28:22,459 --> 01:28:24,626
If this becomes a serve ace,

1949
01:28:25,093 --> 01:28:25,993
it'll be awesome.

1950
01:28:27,526 --> 01:28:28,359
Serve.

1951
01:28:28,359 --> 01:28:30,693
(We must extend our lead here.)

1952
01:28:30,693 --> 01:28:32,226
Oh, no.

1953
01:28:34,959 --> 01:28:38,693
(Homer!)

1954
01:28:39,759 --> 01:28:41,293
I should blame my own mouth.

1955
01:28:41,293 --> 01:28:42,126
I agree.

1956
01:28:43,493 --> 01:28:47,559
Enkhsoyol is also confident
since this is a college-level match.

1957
01:28:48,593 --> 01:28:50,759
(Hitting the net with confidence)

1958
01:28:50,759 --> 01:28:55,259
Myoung Hwa got scolded so much
as her serve didn't reach 65km per hour.

1959
01:28:57,059 --> 01:29:00,526
(And she did something
to be scolded again.)

1960
01:29:01,126 --> 01:29:04,093
(Every time Ho Geun praises,)

1961
01:29:05,626 --> 01:29:09,859
(it immediately leads to a mistake.)

1962
01:29:10,026 --> 01:29:13,926
(Always watch what you say.)

1963
01:29:13,926 --> 01:29:14,893
It's my mistake.

1964
01:29:16,993 --> 01:29:18,793
Focus on reception right away.

1965
01:29:18,818 --> 01:29:19,684
Hey, here.

1966
01:29:25,693 --> 01:29:26,893
A serve by Seo Hyun.

1967
01:29:27,893 --> 01:29:29,559
It'll come to the left.

1968
01:29:31,626 --> 01:29:32,693
Mine.

1969
01:29:32,693 --> 01:29:33,626
Hey, go!

1970
01:29:34,126 --> 01:29:35,259
(The reception was good.)

1971
01:29:35,859 --> 01:29:36,826
Jin.

1972
01:29:36,826 --> 01:29:37,859
And Seung Ju's tip.

1973
01:29:39,159 --> 01:29:40,426
(Covering easily)

1974
01:29:41,593 --> 01:29:44,026
(And the ball goes to Da Bin.)

1975
01:29:44,026 --> 01:29:45,393
Hit it higher.

1976
01:29:48,259 --> 01:29:49,493
(Hitting the blocker's fingertips)

1977
01:29:51,159 --> 01:29:53,326
She dives to make the save.

1978
01:29:53,859 --> 01:29:54,759
And Seung Ju!

1979
01:29:56,793 --> 01:29:58,026
(Covering again)

1980
01:29:59,459 --> 01:30:00,626
It goes toward Da Bin again!

1981
01:30:01,793 --> 01:30:02,759
It's blocked.

1982
01:30:03,426 --> 01:30:04,359
The right!

1983
01:30:05,461 --> 01:30:06,461
(To Eun Ji on the right side)

1984
01:30:06,493 --> 01:30:08,193
It's the right side, this time.

1985
01:30:08,459 --> 01:30:09,893
Block Eun Ji!

1986
01:30:11,593 --> 01:30:12,526
Eun Ji!

1987
01:30:13,793 --> 01:30:15,093
They saved it!

1988
01:30:15,093 --> 01:30:16,026
There you go!

1989
01:30:16,326 --> 01:30:17,659
Hey!

1990
01:30:18,259 --> 01:30:19,459
Seung Ju's dink!

1991
01:30:20,926 --> 01:30:22,393
(They blocked it again!)

1992
01:30:22,726 --> 01:30:24,559
(The ball goes toward Eun Ji once again.)

1993
01:30:26,459 --> 01:30:29,359
(They missed the timing for the block.)

1994
01:30:33,993 --> 01:30:36,159
Eun Ji attacks right from her position!

1995
01:30:40,026 --> 01:30:42,026
Oh, no! Come on!

1996
01:30:43,026 --> 01:30:44,826
The Red Sparks take the lead again.

1997
01:30:47,159 --> 01:30:49,593
- I'm sorry.
- Let's start over.

1998
01:30:52,159 --> 01:30:56,993
Seung Ju, go for a straight attack
this time.

1999
01:30:58,893 --> 01:31:02,826
(The opponent knows
Seung Ju's attack patterns too well.)

2000
01:31:02,993 --> 01:31:04,459
Go for a straight attack.

2001
01:31:05,693 --> 01:31:07,259
Let's just make one more point for now.

2002
01:31:07,259 --> 01:31:09,259
You're doing great now!
Focus on making one point!

2003
01:31:09,259 --> 01:31:11,526
(They need to elevate
their attacking power.)

2004
01:31:15,393 --> 01:31:16,659
The reception is unstable.

2005
01:31:17,293 --> 01:31:18,759
Jin follows it and digs it!

2006
01:31:18,759 --> 01:31:19,726
Nice pass.

2007
01:31:20,393 --> 01:31:21,993
(Now is the time...)

2008
01:31:21,993 --> 01:31:25,826
(to go for a straight attack!)

2009
01:31:26,759 --> 01:31:29,426
(But two blockers had already closed in.)

2010
01:31:29,426 --> 01:31:30,926
Seung Ju's cross-court smash!

2011
01:31:30,926 --> 01:31:32,359
(A cross-court spike is made.)

2012
01:31:33,050 --> 01:31:34,269
(Free ball for Red Sparks)

2013
01:31:34,293 --> 01:31:35,759
They need to defend it here.

2014
01:31:35,759 --> 01:31:37,059
Da Bin with the spike!

2015
01:31:37,726 --> 01:31:40,659
It's out!

2016
01:31:41,526 --> 01:31:47,726
Seung Ju, I told you
to go for a straight attack!

2017
01:31:47,726 --> 01:31:49,159
Why did you target the middle?

2018
01:31:49,159 --> 01:31:50,359
The defender is blocking that area!

2019
01:31:50,359 --> 01:31:51,559
- Okay.
- Make a straight hit.

2020
01:31:51,559 --> 01:31:52,493
Okay.

2021
01:31:52,493 --> 01:31:54,793
- You can angle it slightly if needed.
- Okay.

2022
01:31:55,993 --> 01:31:57,159
The score is 22 to 22.

2023
01:32:04,093 --> 01:32:07,493
(Da Bin goes for it again this time!)

2024
01:32:09,859 --> 01:32:11,226
(They received it!)

2025
01:32:11,226 --> 01:32:12,093
That's it.

2026
01:32:13,793 --> 01:32:17,159
(Yet the ball she received is
going back to Da Bin?)

2027
01:32:18,726 --> 01:32:20,297
(A clean kill!)

2028
01:32:20,321 --> 01:32:21,793
I'm sorry.

2029
01:32:22,051 --> 01:32:23,952
(That was so close!)

2030
01:32:23,976 --> 01:32:25,706
You should've gotten up immediately!

2031
01:32:26,159 --> 01:32:27,426
We need more scores!

2032
01:32:27,426 --> 01:32:29,593
(Da Bin's clever play)

2033
01:32:30,359 --> 01:32:31,793
The score is 22 to 23.

2034
01:32:31,793 --> 01:32:33,159
Focus on the serve!

2035
01:32:34,993 --> 01:32:35,959
Jin.

2036
01:32:36,959 --> 01:32:40,359
Go for a pipe attack
if there's a chance during the rally.

2037
01:32:40,359 --> 01:32:41,826
Do you understand?

2038
01:32:43,459 --> 01:32:47,293
(Let's go for a back-row attack
from the middle again.)

2039
01:32:47,493 --> 01:32:48,359
Serve!

2040
01:32:49,226 --> 01:32:50,226
Da Bin is the server.

2041
01:32:54,826 --> 01:32:55,693
Good.

2042
01:32:56,859 --> 01:32:58,759
(Hye In's stable reception)

2043
01:32:59,559 --> 01:33:01,059
(Jin set the ball to the back row.)

2044
01:33:02,093 --> 01:33:03,526
(And the ball goes to the middle
as planned.)

2045
01:33:03,526 --> 01:33:04,959
(Enkhsoyol's back attack!)

2046
01:33:04,984 --> 01:33:07,184
An attack from the back row!

2047
01:33:08,393 --> 01:33:10,526
(Their attack finally got through.)

2048
01:33:10,526 --> 01:33:12,493
- Out!
- Out.

2049
01:33:15,026 --> 01:33:17,093
- It's out.
- It's ruled out.

2050
01:33:19,326 --> 01:33:20,193
It's in!

2051
01:33:24,193 --> 01:33:25,326
(Requesting a VAR review)

2052
01:33:25,326 --> 01:33:26,926
She called for a challenge right away.

2053
01:33:27,459 --> 01:33:28,693
Was it out?

2054
01:33:31,893 --> 01:33:33,093
It looked like it was out.

2055
01:33:34,493 --> 01:33:35,326
Please.

2056
01:33:45,093 --> 01:33:46,754
It was in.

2057
01:33:47,777 --> 01:33:48,777
It's in.

2058
01:33:49,217 --> 01:33:52,284
(Cheering)

2059
01:33:53,084 --> 01:33:55,484
(I told you it's in.)

2060
01:33:56,431 --> 01:34:01,064
(It's in, Enkhsoyol!)

2061
01:34:03,454 --> 01:34:05,588
Nice one, Enkhsoyol!

2062
01:34:06,821 --> 01:34:09,554
- I can't believe Enkhsoyol did it.
- Good. She didn't expect this either.

2063
01:34:09,554 --> 01:34:10,554
(Yay!)

2064
01:34:10,821 --> 01:34:12,121
From now on,

2065
01:34:12,921 --> 01:34:15,049
they shouldn't be catching up
but leading the game.

2066
01:34:15,688 --> 01:34:17,088
Nice serve!

2067
01:34:17,121 --> 01:34:18,721
(We got the momentum back.)

2068
01:34:19,321 --> 01:34:20,821
(Lee Jin serves.)

2069
01:34:20,854 --> 01:34:22,254
Let's go!

2070
01:34:23,354 --> 01:34:24,354
Mine!

2071
01:34:24,354 --> 01:34:25,488
The reception is shaky!

2072
01:34:25,488 --> 01:34:27,354
(The serve shook the reception.)

2073
01:34:29,221 --> 01:34:31,188
- Pyo Seung Ju!
- It's their chance.

2074
01:34:31,188 --> 01:34:33,121
(This is their chance!)

2075
01:34:33,454 --> 01:34:35,688
(Enkhsoyol runs.)

2076
01:34:36,629 --> 01:34:37,763
(And so does Koo Hye In?)

2077
01:34:37,788 --> 01:34:39,854
I'm sorry!

2078
01:34:39,854 --> 01:34:41,321
(Their routes are tangled.)

2079
01:34:41,488 --> 01:34:42,521
Hey!

2080
01:34:43,107 --> 01:34:43,998
(Swearing)

2081
01:34:45,366 --> 01:34:47,633
(And the free ball goes
to the Red Sparks.)

2082
01:34:48,234 --> 01:34:50,467
(Shin Eun Ji leaps!)

2083
01:34:51,727 --> 01:34:54,993
(They succeed in blocking.)

2084
01:34:54,993 --> 01:34:56,027
(Whistling)

2085
01:34:56,360 --> 01:34:57,393
It's out?

2086
01:34:58,493 --> 01:35:00,060
What? No!

2087
01:35:00,060 --> 01:35:02,260
- Oh, dear.
- It's a net touch!

2088
01:35:03,393 --> 01:35:07,127
(What a blessing!)

2089
01:35:10,960 --> 01:35:11,993
Me?

2090
01:35:11,993 --> 01:35:14,660
No. I swear I didn't touch the net!

2091
01:35:15,593 --> 01:35:16,727
(Press it.)

2092
01:35:18,960 --> 01:35:19,960
She didn't touch it.

2093
01:35:19,960 --> 01:35:22,927
(Coach Kim asks for a video review
of the net touch.)

2094
01:35:22,927 --> 01:35:24,393
The Pilseung Wonder Dogs...

2095
01:35:24,427 --> 01:35:27,493
requested a video review
about the net touch.

2096
01:35:32,660 --> 01:35:34,393
- Okay.
- I see.

2097
01:35:34,427 --> 01:35:36,727
The net doesn't shake at all.

2098
01:35:36,727 --> 01:35:38,327
In fact, she kept a distance from it.

2099
01:35:39,127 --> 01:35:42,293
The video review rules it as no touch.

2100
01:35:43,127 --> 01:35:44,960
One more!

2101
01:35:45,527 --> 01:35:46,660
Good.

2102
01:35:47,093 --> 01:35:48,660
That shocked me.

2103
01:35:48,927 --> 01:35:50,527
(My heart.)

2104
01:35:50,560 --> 01:35:52,093
This is a replay.

2105
01:35:52,327 --> 01:35:54,393
We go back to a previous rally.

2106
01:35:55,460 --> 01:35:56,627
One more.

2107
01:35:56,627 --> 01:35:59,160
(They set the disappointment aside
and focus again.)

2108
01:36:00,027 --> 01:36:03,393
The game continues
with the score of 23 to 23.

2109
01:36:09,160 --> 01:36:12,293
(The ball goes to Gwak Seon Ok.)

2110
01:36:12,760 --> 01:36:14,327
(It broke through their block?)

2111
01:36:15,560 --> 01:36:17,693
(They fail to defend.)

2112
01:36:22,027 --> 01:36:24,427
That was our point.

2113
01:36:24,453 --> 01:36:26,420
Send the ball back once.

2114
01:36:26,460 --> 01:36:27,960
(They lose the crucial point.)

2115
01:36:27,993 --> 01:36:29,493
It's 23 to 24.

2116
01:36:29,527 --> 01:36:31,693
The Red Sparks' set point.

2117
01:36:32,927 --> 01:36:34,827
(But they are only a point apart.)

2118
01:36:35,260 --> 01:36:38,327
Jin, in the middle.

2119
01:36:39,193 --> 01:36:41,427
(We'll catch them up again
with a back attack.)

2120
01:36:45,960 --> 01:36:47,227
Go!

2121
01:36:48,793 --> 01:36:51,627
(Koo Hye In receives it well.)

2122
01:36:51,660 --> 01:36:53,827
(Lee Jin sets the ball to the back!)

2123
01:36:55,193 --> 01:36:56,560
Come on!

2124
01:36:57,320 --> 01:36:59,320
(The Wonder Dogs are on fire.)

2125
01:36:59,720 --> 01:37:01,720
(Will they be able to win?)

2126
01:37:02,153 --> 01:37:04,686
Is volleyball hard for you?
The game isn't finished yet.

2127
01:37:05,086 --> 01:37:08,353
(Easy play, once the pro realizes
their potential)

2128
01:37:10,253 --> 01:37:12,420
(Will the Wonder Dogs fall...)

2129
01:37:12,420 --> 01:37:13,720
(in the end?)

2130
01:37:13,753 --> 01:37:15,886
(Guys.)

2131
01:37:15,920 --> 01:37:17,220
(It's great, isn't it?)

2132
01:37:17,253 --> 01:37:18,853
Be confident. It's okay.

2133
01:37:18,853 --> 01:37:20,420
Forget everything you did before.

2134
01:37:20,420 --> 01:37:22,953
We should think of what to do now.

2135
01:37:23,353 --> 01:37:24,986
- You've got this. Okay?
- Yes.

2136
01:37:25,386 --> 01:37:26,920
(Let's do this now,)

2137
01:37:27,086 --> 01:37:28,420
(before we regret it!)

2138
01:37:28,886 --> 01:37:31,086
(If you're a pro team,)

2139
01:37:31,120 --> 01:37:32,853
(then we're the Wonder Dogs.)

2140
01:37:33,120 --> 01:37:34,786
(The Wonder Dogs' wonderful take off)

2141
01:37:35,520 --> 01:37:37,253
(The underdogs' determination...)

2142
01:37:37,786 --> 01:37:40,920
(shakes the pro team.)

2143
01:37:41,020 --> 01:37:42,686
What are you doing?

2144
01:37:42,986 --> 01:37:46,253
(The underdogs' counterattack begins now!)
